WEBVTT

00:00:17.390 --> 00:00:20.930
<i>Raccoon, Raccoon</i>
<i>Come on out and play</i>

00:00:21.390 --> 00:00:24.440
<i>I can't right now, I'm eating</i>

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:26.440
<i>What is it you're eating?</i>

00:00:26.900 --> 00:00:28.770
<i>Pickled plums and radish</i>

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:30.730
<i>How about some for me?</i>

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:33.900
<i>Hey, don't be so greedy</i>

00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:51.460
<i>We raccoons</i>
<i>have always lived near humans.</i>

00:00:53.050 --> 00:00:55.970
<i>Not to steal their food. Not at all.</i>

00:00:56.050 --> 00:00:58.050
<i>Where there are paddies and fields,</i>

00:00:58.140 --> 00:01:02.180
<i>there are frogs and grasshoppers,</i>
<i>mice and moles.</i>

00:01:02.270 --> 00:01:04.430
<i>There's fruit,</i>
<i>like persimmons and mulberries.</i>

00:01:04.810 --> 00:01:08.060
<i>There's much more food than in the woods.</i>

00:01:09.230 --> 00:01:13.530
<i>Last spring, the old farmhouse</i>
<i>was suddenly abandoned.</i>

00:01:13.940 --> 00:01:18.620
<i>It looked like no one was coming back,</i>
<i>so we all moved in.</i>

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:33.380
<i>We spent a really wonderful year there.</i>

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:37.180
<i>Living in a house</i>
<i>with a garden was like a dream.</i>

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:38.340
<i>But then...</i>

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:58.700
<i>We raccoons usually don't make a fuss</i>
<i>over territory, but this was different.</i>

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:02.450
<i>Wherever we went looking for food,</i>
<i>we ran into other raccoons.</i>

00:02:02.830 --> 00:02:05.830
<i>There were quarrels,</i>
<i>and fights over burrows...</i>

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:07.040
<i>until one day...</i>

00:02:09.500 --> 00:02:11.500
<i>Autumn, year 31 of the Pom Poko era.</i>

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:15.510
<i>On the newly logged border</i>
<i>between Taka and Suzu Woods,</i>

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:19.510
<i>the raccoons of Tama Hills</i>
<i>gathered for their final battle.</i>

00:02:50.540 --> 00:02:53.750
<i>The red army was led by Gonta,</i>
<i>a fearsome raccoon from Taka.</i>

00:02:54.840 --> 00:02:58.340
<i>The blue army was led by Seizaemon,</i>
<i>an elder from Suzu.</i>

00:03:02.640 --> 00:03:05.050
<i>Now, it's a little-known fact,</i>

00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:08.390
<i>but when humans aren't around,</i>

00:03:08.470 --> 00:03:13.020
<i>raccoons walk on two legs,</i>
<i>just as you see here.</i>

00:04:05.620 --> 00:04:09.450
<i>The battle was hard-fought,</i>
<i>but it did not last long.</i>

00:04:10.620 --> 00:04:16.380
<i>Fight, fight! Taka!</i>
<i>Fight, fight! Suzu!</i>

00:04:16.630 --> 00:04:19.880
<i>Red wins, blue wins</i>
<i>Both of you lose</i>

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:22.380
<i>Slaughter the losing raccoons</i>

00:04:22.630 --> 00:04:28.430
<i>Taka loses today</i>
<i>Suzu loses tomorrow</i>

00:04:28.550 --> 00:04:31.390
<i>The raccoons have nowhere to go</i>

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.390
<i>Where can the raccoons go to?</i>

00:04:34.480 --> 00:04:37.440
<i>There's nowhere for them to go</i>

00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.820
<i>Whether red wins or blue wins</i>
<i>Both sides lose</i>

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:43.400
<i>Kill the losing raccoons!</i>

00:04:43.490 --> 00:04:46.450
<i>It's for the greater good</i>

00:04:46.820 --> 00:04:49.410
<i>There are too many of them</i>

00:04:49.530 --> 00:04:52.000
<i>Fewer raccoons is better for all</i>

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.750
<i>The rest of you, control yourselves</i>

00:04:55.000 --> 00:04:57.000
<i>Stop having children</i>

00:04:57.080 --> 00:04:59.670
<i>Have more children</i>
<i>And you'll lose everything</i>

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.010
<i>Your homes are disappearing</i>
<i>And that's a fact</i>

00:05:06.430 --> 00:05:08.590
<i>Granny Oroku was right.</i>

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:11.930
<i>The raccoons were stunned</i>
<i>by the desolation around them.</i>

00:05:12.430 --> 00:05:14.100
<i>Their woods were disappearing.</i>

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:16.730
<i>A chilling panorama of denuded,</i>
<i>flattened hills</i>

00:05:16.810 --> 00:05:19.270
<i>stretched as far as the eye could see.</i>

00:05:19.940 --> 00:05:21.610
This is madness!

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:24.360
It's no time for us to be fighting!

00:05:27.910 --> 00:05:31.200
<i>In those days, Japan was entering</i>
<i>a golden age of economic growth.</i>

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:33.580
<i>Demand for housing around Tokyo exploded.</i>

00:05:33.660 --> 00:05:37.170
<i>Lots of farmland and forest disappeared</i>
<i>in waves of uncontrolled development.</i>

00:05:37.540 --> 00:05:44.210
<i>As Tokyo grew, it gnawed the land</i>
<i>in random patterns like a huge insect.</i>

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.840
<i>Then in 1967, the city fathers</i>
<i>hit on a better idea:</i>

00:05:46.970 --> 00:05:50.010
<i>A plan for a new suburb of Tokyo</i>
<i>called Tama New Town.</i>

00:05:50.430 --> 00:05:55.600
<i>Over 300,000 people would populate</i>
<i>an area of 3,000 hectares.</i>

00:05:56.100 --> 00:05:59.980
<i>Forests would be cleared,</i>
<i>hills flattened, valleys filled,</i>

00:06:00.060 --> 00:06:03.360
<i>farms and fields obliterated,</i>
<i>old farmhouses demolished.</i>

00:06:03.440 --> 00:06:08.700
<i>Tama Hills would be transformed</i>
<i>into an enormous construction site</i>

00:06:08.780 --> 00:06:13.200
<i>to create a model bedroom town</i>
<i>for Tokyo's workers.</i>

00:06:13.280 --> 00:06:16.370
<i>It was the largest urban development</i>
<i>project in history.</i>

00:06:19.330 --> 00:06:22.130
You've got to hand it to these humans.
They're really something.

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:26.510
We always thought
they were animals just like us,

00:06:27.050 --> 00:06:28.550
but now we know we were wrong.

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:34.390
They must be even more powerful
than the gods.

00:06:39.270 --> 00:06:42.980
<i>Raccoon clans from all over Tama Hills</i>

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.570
<i>gathered secretly late one night</i>
<i>at the old abandoned Manpuku Temple,</i>

00:06:47.650 --> 00:06:49.990
<i>deep in the forest.</i>

00:06:50.280 --> 00:06:52.740
<i>By unanimous agreement of all present,</i>

00:06:52.820 --> 00:06:55.080
<i>the meeting was chaired by Tsurukame Osho,</i>

00:06:55.200 --> 00:06:57.330
<i>the temple's 105-year-old</i>
<i>resident raccoon.</i>

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:00.250
...so in view of the current difficulties,

00:07:00.670 --> 00:07:05.000
we must abandon our nocturnal habits

00:07:05.420 --> 00:07:09.840
and be prepared to act
at any time of the day or night.

00:07:09.970 --> 00:07:11.010
<i>Amid some confusion,</i>

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:14.430
<i>the assembly agreed</i>
<i>on a policy to stop the development.</i>

00:07:14.720 --> 00:07:18.640
That makes it unanimous!

00:07:20.350 --> 00:07:22.350
<i>The raccoons went home,</i>

00:07:22.850 --> 00:07:25.650
<i>while the clan elders worked out</i>
<i>a specific course of action.</i>

00:07:28.190 --> 00:07:32.160
<i>The elders settled on a five-year plan</i>

00:07:32.490 --> 00:07:34.820
<i>to revive the neglected art</i>
<i>of shape-shifting</i>

00:07:34.950 --> 00:07:36.160
<i>and study the ways of humans.</i>

00:07:36.870 --> 00:07:39.000
<i>They invited</i>
<i>renowned shape-shifting practitioners</i>

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.660
<i>from Sado and Shikoku islands,</i>

00:07:40.910 --> 00:07:43.790
<i>where the art was most advanced,</i>
<i>to teach the young raccoons.</i>

00:07:43.880 --> 00:07:44.830
YASHIIMA - SABURŌ

00:07:44.920 --> 00:07:47.090
<i>But in view of the difficulties</i>

00:07:49.210 --> 00:07:52.300
<i>and danger posed by the long journeys</i>
<i>to fetch these teachers,</i>

00:07:52.380 --> 00:07:55.140
<i>no one wanted to go.</i>
<i>So, they all pretended to fall asleep.</i>

00:07:55.850 --> 00:07:58.600
I suppose we'll just have to wait
for the youngsters

00:07:58.680 --> 00:08:00.060
to acquire the skills on their own.

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:03.850
Agreed!

00:08:05.770 --> 00:08:08.860
<i>The McDonald's hamburgers</i>
<i>provided to fuel the discussion</i>

00:08:08.940 --> 00:08:12.360
<i>were enthusiastically received.</i>

00:08:12.610 --> 00:08:15.410
<i>And with that,</i>
<i>the council of elders concluded.</i>

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.580
REVIVE SHAPE-SHIFTING
STUDY HUMANS

00:08:27.340 --> 00:08:29.210
NO DUMPING

00:08:29.300 --> 00:08:33.670
<i>Keeping close track of human acitivity</i>
<i>was of the utmost importance,</i>

00:08:33.840 --> 00:08:36.720
<i>so the raccoons decided</i>
<i>to set up a television set</i>

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.350
<i>in their headquarters,</i>
<i>the main hall of Manpuku Temple.</i>

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:51.400
-<i>Good evening.</i>
-Good evening!

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:55.400
<i>The arrival of the television</i>
<i>provoked great interest.</i>

00:09:00.280 --> 00:09:03.410
<i>The headquarters at Manpuku Temple</i>
<i>were soon crowded with visitors</i>

00:09:03.700 --> 00:09:07.080
<i>who were there just to spend the day</i>
<i>watching television.</i>

00:09:09.290 --> 00:09:12.880
Shape-shifting requires the highest
degree of mental concentration.

00:09:12.960 --> 00:09:17.260
It means changing
one's very cells in an instant.

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:20.050
Truly, this is nature's greatest miracle.

00:09:20.470 --> 00:09:25.850
Lesser forms of transformation can be
achieved by such animals as chameleons.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:31.230
But only raccoons, foxes and some
old cats can practice real shape-shifting.

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:32.570
YIN YANG
SHAPE-SHIFTING

00:09:33.400 --> 00:09:34.740
Gonta!

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:38.450
That you can assume
such an appearance, even for a moment,

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:43.040
proves you've taken the first steps on
the path, whether you realise it or not.

00:09:43.540 --> 00:09:45.960
If one studies hard and grasps the basics,

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.040
any raccoon can learn to shape-shift.
At least in theory.

00:09:52.380 --> 00:09:55.380
Allow me to demonstrate!

00:09:57.010 --> 00:09:59.090
Aren't you going to put a leaf
on your head?

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.010
That's for beginners!

00:10:09.600 --> 00:10:11.190
It's been a long time!

00:10:11.610 --> 00:10:13.980
And a one, and a two!

00:10:14.940 --> 00:10:17.450
<i>With Granny Oroku as their instructor,</i>

00:10:17.530 --> 00:10:20.320
<i>the raccoons made steady progress</i>
<i>in the art of shape-shifting.</i>

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:26.580
<i>Young raccoons from every clan burned</i>
<i>with desire to hone their skills.</i>

00:10:28.410 --> 00:10:29.920
Bravo, Shokichi!

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:37.760
-Gotcha!
-Gotcha!

00:10:38.170 --> 00:10:39.510
Gotcha!

00:10:42.430 --> 00:10:45.810
<i>I've been interested in humans</i>
<i>and their ways ever since I was a child.</i>

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:50.230
<i>As a rule we weren't supposed</i>
<i>to approach them,</i>

00:10:50.310 --> 00:10:53.900
<i>but for my late father, I think that</i>
<i>just sharpened his interest.</i>

00:10:54.730 --> 00:10:58.570
<i>Careful observation of humans is</i>
<i>a basic requirement for shape-shifting,</i>

00:10:58.650 --> 00:11:02.070
<i>so I'm sure he thought getting close</i>
<i>to them would prove useful.</i>

00:11:22.090 --> 00:11:25.760
<i>It goes without saying that some</i>
<i>of our raccoons were not good students.</i>

00:11:26.100 --> 00:11:29.640
<i>In fact, many of them</i>
<i>simply couldn't manage at all.</i>

00:11:34.400 --> 00:11:38.690
<i>Shape-shifting requires rigorous</i>
<i>physical and mental discipline.</i>

00:11:38.780 --> 00:11:42.150
<i>Naturally this discouraged</i>
<i>many of the raccoons,</i>

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.280
<i>who unlike foxes,</i>
<i>are inclined to be rather lazy.</i>

00:11:48.450 --> 00:11:49.660
Hey!

00:11:56.460 --> 00:11:57.380
Ponkichi!

00:11:57.460 --> 00:12:00.710
<i>All the arhats are here</i>
<i>Turn them</i>

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:02.800
<i>Turn, turn, turn, turn</i>

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.390
<i>Back then all I thought about</i>
<i>was shape-shifting.</i>

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:07.640
<i>I never dreamed my childhood pal Ponkichi</i>

00:12:07.720 --> 00:12:11.890
<i>wanted nothing more than to live</i>
<i>like a normal raccoon.</i>

00:12:14.350 --> 00:12:17.310
...so when the traveler
reached the mountain pass,

00:12:17.610 --> 00:12:20.320
he saw the pine tree

00:12:20.730 --> 00:12:24.610
seemed to have grown an extra branch.

00:12:25.530 --> 00:12:26.530
Now, this was odd.

00:12:26.620 --> 00:12:30.490
The traveler said to himself, "There was
no branch on that side last time."

00:12:30.580 --> 00:12:35.370
And lo and behold!
The branch switched sides.

00:12:36.540 --> 00:12:39.630
Seeing this, the traveler said aloud,

00:12:39.710 --> 00:12:42.760
"That's not right either.
There were branches on both sides."

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.930
And sure enough,
branches sprouted on both sides.

00:12:46.430 --> 00:12:47.760
The next instant, boom!

00:12:47.850 --> 00:12:52.060
Something fell!
What was it, do you suppose?

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:53.350
A raccoon!

00:12:53.850 --> 00:12:56.980
Right! And why did he fall? Gonta?

00:12:57.650 --> 00:13:00.360
He was a klutz. I'd never fall.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:06.200
That's the spirit!
Sasuke, why do you think he fell?

00:13:06.610 --> 00:13:09.200
He had to let go of the tree
to make two branches.

00:13:09.530 --> 00:13:14.210
Very good! And what is the moral
of this story? Shokichi?

00:13:14.620 --> 00:13:18.250
It doesn't pay to take
what humans say literally.

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:22.710
That's correct.
We raccoons are naturally good-natured.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:25.670
We get carried away!
We try too hard to please!

00:13:26.010 --> 00:13:29.390
This is where we go wrong. Do you see?

00:13:29.470 --> 00:13:30.970
Yes, Tsurukame Osho!

00:13:31.470 --> 00:13:38.230
So if I were to say: "Mr. Raccoon,
Mr. Raccoon, come out and play"?

00:13:38.650 --> 00:13:42.360
<i>We're in the middle of a lesson now!</i>

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:47.360
See? You're already getting carried away!
This is what worries me!

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:08.430
<i>As the raccoons worked to understand</i>
<i>humans and practice shape-shifting,</i>

00:14:08.510 --> 00:14:10.010
<i>winter turned to spring.</i>

00:14:10.090 --> 00:14:12.930
<i>The plum trees blossomed,</i>
<i>and love was in the air.</i>

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:17.640
<i>But most raccoons heeded</i>
<i>Granny Oroku's order to remain chaste</i>

00:14:17.730 --> 00:14:23.520
<i>and to avoid having children</i>
<i>until everyone's homes were safe again.</i>

00:14:24.190 --> 00:14:28.650
<i>They suppressed their maternal instincts</i>

00:14:28.740 --> 00:14:32.990
<i>and firmly rejected</i>
<i>the males' clumsy efforts to woo them.</i>

00:14:38.460 --> 00:14:42.500
<i>Meanwhile, the massive</i>
<i>development project was picking up steam.</i>

00:14:42.590 --> 00:14:44.500
<i>Woods were cleared, the earth was scoured,</i>

00:14:44.590 --> 00:14:46.340
<i>and construction sites multiplied.</i>

00:14:46.710 --> 00:14:49.170
<i>The raccoons,</i>
<i>filled with anger and sadness,</i>

00:14:49.260 --> 00:14:51.970
<i>called these sites "bald hills."</i>

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:57.390
<i>Mr. Postman, you dropped something</i>

00:14:57.470 --> 00:15:01.560
<i>Freed from the work of child-rearing,</i>

00:15:02.060 --> 00:15:05.650
<i>some of the females</i>
<i>started to practice shape-shifting too.</i>

00:15:06.820 --> 00:15:09.700
<i>When males tried to pass themselves</i>
<i>off as women or children,</i>

00:15:09.780 --> 00:15:11.990
<i>the overall effect was not quite right.</i>

00:15:12.070 --> 00:15:14.990
<i>With the participation of the females,</i>
<i>this problem was solved.</i>

00:15:16.040 --> 00:15:20.160
<i>Naturally, some of the females wanted</i>
<i>to try their hand at turning into males.</i>

00:15:23.170 --> 00:15:27.920
Ah, I'd like the males
to stay after class today.

00:15:28.800 --> 00:15:34.390
<i>One day, Tsurukame Osho</i>
<i>gave a special lecture for the males.</i>

00:15:35.550 --> 00:15:42.060
Now then, what do you think
the carpet you are all sitting on is?

00:15:42.600 --> 00:15:45.980
I may as well tell you. It's my testicles!

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:51.110
It's exactly eight mats.
And I'll prove it!

00:16:03.290 --> 00:16:07.540
<i>The time finally came for the students</i>
<i>to test their skills in the real world.</i>

00:16:09.380 --> 00:16:11.840
<i>The exercise was conducted</i>
<i>like a driving lesson.</i>

00:16:11.920 --> 00:16:15.430
<i>Each student was accompanied</i>
<i>by an advanced partner,</i>

00:16:15.510 --> 00:16:19.560
<i>in case of unforeseen problems</i>
<i>or someone seeing through their disguise.</i>

00:16:50.750 --> 00:16:54.590
<i>Shape-shifting requires</i>
<i>large amounts of energy,</i>

00:16:54.880 --> 00:16:57.300
<i>especially when assuming human form.</i>

00:16:59.180 --> 00:17:01.640
<i>The dark circles</i>
<i>raccoons have around their eyes</i>

00:17:01.720 --> 00:17:06.230
<i>are the result of sheer fatigue.</i>

00:17:06.310 --> 00:17:08.650
<i>Even experienced shape-shifters</i>

00:17:08.730 --> 00:17:11.650
<i>have to secretly carry special herbs</i>

00:17:11.730 --> 00:17:14.150
<i>to replenish their strength</i>
<i>at a moment's notice.</i>

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:16.030
<i>Otherwise, out pops the tail,</i>

00:17:16.110 --> 00:17:19.580
<i>and the next thing you know,</i>
<i>they're back to their original form.</i>

00:17:21.490 --> 00:17:23.250
<i>Recently raccoons have discovered</i>

00:17:23.330 --> 00:17:28.380
<i>that instant energy drinks widely sold</i>
<i>in stores are a good pick-me-up.</i>

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.590
<i>To graduate</i>
<i>from the shape-shifting course,</i>

00:17:32.920 --> 00:17:34.970
<i>students had to pass one final test:</i>

00:17:35.050 --> 00:17:38.680
<i>they had to go out and earn</i>
<i>at least 1,000 yen through honest labor.</i>

00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:40.600
Help!

00:17:41.430 --> 00:17:44.430
<i>Some raccoons got together and took turns</i>
<i>impersonating the same human.</i>

00:17:44.560 --> 00:17:45.680
Are you all right?

00:17:45.850 --> 00:17:49.150
<i>Others transformed themselves</i>
<i>into monks with begging bowls.</i>

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:54.190
<i>Some females worked in clubs and raked in</i>
<i>money drinking with customers.</i>

00:17:54.820 --> 00:17:58.160
<i>Another raccoon won a fortune</i>
<i>at the pachinko parlor.</i>

00:17:58.240 --> 00:17:59.070
COLLECTION BOX

00:17:59.160 --> 00:18:01.990
<i>One tricky raccoon</i>
<i>burgled a temple donation box,</i>

00:18:02.080 --> 00:18:03.790
<i>but all he got was small change.</i>

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:08.040
<i>So he transformed some leaves into bills,</i>
<i>but Oroku saw right through him.</i>

00:18:10.000 --> 00:18:14.460
I told you modern shape-shifting
forbids turning leaves into money!

00:18:22.100 --> 00:18:25.270
<i>One day, an urgent report interrupted</i>
<i>Gonta's training at headquarters.</i>

00:18:25.350 --> 00:18:29.060
<i>He hurried home</i>
<i>to Taka Woods to face tragedy.</i>

00:18:29.440 --> 00:18:34.860
<i>More than half his childhood home</i>
<i>had already been ravaged by construction.</i>

00:18:37.490 --> 00:18:39.070
<i>Gonta went mad with grief.</i>

00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:41.200
<i>He raced back to headquarters</i>

00:18:41.280 --> 00:18:44.240
<i>and forced Tsurukame Osho</i>
<i>to call a meeting of the clan elders,</i>

00:18:44.370 --> 00:18:47.450
<i>where he called for a strategy</i>
<i>of violent attacks on the humans.</i>

00:18:48.370 --> 00:18:51.250
-I'm completely against this.
-Why?

00:18:51.630 --> 00:18:55.340
The time is not ripe. We're still
in the first year of the Five-Year Plan.

00:18:55.550 --> 00:18:59.590
We've all completed our training.
There's a lot we can do right now!

00:19:00.130 --> 00:19:05.850
What do you think, Granny? Do you think
these youngsters are up to it?

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:09.520
True, they've mastered the basics, but...

00:19:09.810 --> 00:19:11.100
But?

00:19:11.190 --> 00:19:16.690
They lack experience.
One slip and they'll be exposed.

00:19:16.820 --> 00:19:18.440
Gonta, I have to ask you this.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:21.450
I think your anger at what happened
to Taka Woods

00:19:21.530 --> 00:19:25.660
is clouding your judgment.

00:19:25.780 --> 00:19:26.870
Isn't that so?

00:19:28.120 --> 00:19:30.620
I swear there is
absolutely no truth to that.

00:19:31.120 --> 00:19:34.880
I'm thinking of the welfare
of all the raccoons of Tama.

00:19:35.170 --> 00:19:37.840
What do you mean, everyone's welfare?

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:42.840
Don't forget, Gonta's the one
who tried to take over Suzu Woods!

00:19:42.930 --> 00:19:43.930
Shut up!

00:19:44.260 --> 00:19:47.930
Even if no one's for it, we raccoons
of Taka are going ahead anyway.

00:19:48.100 --> 00:19:51.100
If Gonta's that determined,
I'm going to help him!

00:19:51.190 --> 00:19:52.980
You too, Shokichi?

00:19:53.310 --> 00:19:54.810
Thank you!

00:19:55.770 --> 00:20:00.240
It's too late to stop us now!

00:20:00.490 --> 00:20:02.320
Not so fast!

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:05.120
Don't try to stop us, Granny!

00:20:05.530 --> 00:20:09.750
Just this once,
I'll teach you a special technique!

00:20:13.080 --> 00:20:15.630
If you bungle this,

00:20:15.710 --> 00:20:19.130
you won't return to your original form
for five days.

00:20:20.420 --> 00:20:21.920
So, what is it?

00:20:22.840 --> 00:20:25.180
A dead fox!

00:20:25.430 --> 00:20:27.350
<i>Summer, year 32 of the Pom Poko era.</i>

00:20:27.720 --> 00:20:31.600
<i>Ten young volunteers</i>
<i>led by Gonta of Taka Woods</i>

00:20:31.680 --> 00:20:34.190
<i>set out to apply</i>
<i>their new skills in shape-shifting</i>

00:20:34.520 --> 00:20:37.650
<i>with a series of desperate</i>
<i>surprise attacks on the humans.</i>

00:20:38.150 --> 00:20:40.780
<i>The raccoons were fighting back at last.</i>

00:20:54.040 --> 00:20:55.710
-Here they come!
-They're coming!

00:21:00.340 --> 00:21:03.970
Keep going! Keep going!

00:21:09.640 --> 00:21:11.180
We did it!

00:21:57.100 --> 00:21:58.900
<i>Multiple accidents at construction site.</i>

00:21:58.980 --> 00:22:02.570
<i>Disaster struck Tama New Town</i>
<i>development site at approximately 2:30 pm.</i>

00:22:02.650 --> 00:22:07.570
<i>A series of landslides and accidents</i>
<i>killed three workers, injured two,</i>

00:22:07.650 --> 00:22:11.990
<i>and destroyed</i>
<i>a residence under construction.</i>

00:22:12.080 --> 00:22:13.080
LIVE

00:22:13.160 --> 00:22:17.660
<i>Police suspect reduced visibility</i>
<i>and unstable ground from heavy rains.</i>

00:22:17.750 --> 00:22:23.750
<i>The widespread, simultaneous nature</i>
<i>of the accidents is raising concern.</i>

00:22:23.840 --> 00:22:26.760
<i>There may be fundamental flaws</i>
<i>with the development plan.</i>

00:22:26.840 --> 00:22:32.800
<i>Some local residents</i>
<i>are calling for a review of the plan.</i>

00:22:35.970 --> 00:22:38.230
Hold on, everyone!

00:22:38.350 --> 00:22:40.520
I think we should take a moment

00:22:40.690 --> 00:22:44.400
to remember the poor humans

00:22:44.480 --> 00:22:47.780
who died in this operation.

00:22:48.070 --> 00:22:50.200
Osho is right.

00:22:50.410 --> 00:22:56.290
Let's observe a minute of silent prayer
for the unfortunate victims.

00:22:56.500 --> 00:22:59.290
Agreed! A minute of silence!

00:22:59.620 --> 00:23:00.920
All pray!

00:23:04.670 --> 00:23:06.460
Namo Amitabha, Namo Amitabha,

00:23:06.840 --> 00:23:08.920
Namo Amitabha, Namo Amitabha...

00:23:20.350 --> 00:23:22.440
What a success!

00:23:53.640 --> 00:23:55.220
Look, it's Gonta!

00:23:57.510 --> 00:23:59.270
The heroes have returned!

00:24:03.230 --> 00:24:05.230
You really did it, Shokichi!

00:24:07.110 --> 00:24:12.860
You youngsters have restored hope
in this old heart of mine.

00:24:13.780 --> 00:24:16.620
That was only the beginning!
Today was just a practice run!

00:24:17.450 --> 00:24:20.290
Raccoons, the war has started!

00:24:20.370 --> 00:24:25.580
We must kill, crush,
and mangle every human we can,

00:24:25.670 --> 00:24:28.090
until they are driven from Tama Hills!

00:24:28.170 --> 00:24:30.590
Shokichi, you should say something too!

00:24:31.050 --> 00:24:32.340
And let's plant trees!

00:24:32.920 --> 00:24:36.640
Lots and lots
of our favorite persimmon trees!

00:24:38.640 --> 00:24:41.310
<i>Little persimmon seeds</i>
<i>Send out your shoots</i>

00:24:41.560 --> 00:24:45.100
<i>We'll have all the persimmons we can eat</i>

00:24:45.520 --> 00:24:47.480
Out with the humans!

00:24:47.770 --> 00:24:50.030
Slaughter the humans!

00:24:50.110 --> 00:24:55.860
Okay, okay, okay. But first,
we must celebrate this auspicious victory.

00:24:56.360 --> 00:24:58.870
You know, something worries me.

00:24:59.580 --> 00:25:00.830
What?

00:25:01.750 --> 00:25:04.250
Are we really going to drive out
all the humans?

00:25:04.540 --> 00:25:05.870
Of course!

00:25:05.960 --> 00:25:08.880
Can't we let a few of them stay,
the way it used to be?

00:25:09.250 --> 00:25:12.300
No way!
The two-legs are our sworn enemies.

00:25:12.380 --> 00:25:15.380
They're vermin. We've got to get rid
of them once and for all!

00:25:16.050 --> 00:25:20.680
I see. I mean, look, I hate humans too.

00:25:21.140 --> 00:25:27.480
Well, some of them are not so bad.
I mean, I really do hate them. But...

00:25:27.980 --> 00:25:29.060
But what?

00:25:29.480 --> 00:25:35.030
But if we get rid of them all,
we'll never eat tempura again!

00:25:36.660 --> 00:25:37.570
Or sardines!

00:25:38.820 --> 00:25:39.700
Or corn!

00:25:40.120 --> 00:25:46.370
Hamburgers! Donuts! Fried chicken!
Potato chips! Pizza!

00:25:47.330 --> 00:25:48.460
I can taste it!

00:25:49.710 --> 00:25:53.960
Well then, Gonta, shall we let
a few of the humans stay?

00:25:55.340 --> 00:25:56.470
I guess it can't be helped.

00:25:59.140 --> 00:26:01.350
Hooray for Gon! Lift him up, fellows!

00:26:02.470 --> 00:26:07.350
<i>The moon, moon, moon shines bright</i>

00:26:07.980 --> 00:26:13.820
<i>Over Man-Man-Manpuku Temple</i>

00:26:13.900 --> 00:26:17.490
<i>All our friends are here tonight</i>
<i>Pun Poko pun pun, pun pun</i>

00:26:17.610 --> 00:26:20.160
<i>We'll show the world</i>
<i>What Tsurukame Osho can do</i>

00:26:20.240 --> 00:26:22.700
<i>Come on, come on</i>
<i>All our friends are here tonight</i>

00:26:23.240 --> 00:26:27.080
<i>Come on, come on</i>
<i>All our friends are here tonight</i>

00:26:27.160 --> 00:26:28.830
<i>A government spokesman stressed</i>

00:26:28.920 --> 00:26:32.920
<i>that the project is an urgent necessity</i>
<i>for the people of Tokyo,</i>

00:26:33.040 --> 00:26:36.420
<i>and that today's accidents will not affect</i>

00:26:36.550 --> 00:26:40.680
<i>the government's determination</i>
<i>to carry out the construction.</i>

00:26:41.180 --> 00:26:42.430
What?

00:26:46.020 --> 00:26:47.600
<i>It was a very unfortunate accident.</i>

00:26:47.680 --> 00:26:51.770
<i>Poor Gonta,</i>
<i>the driving force behind the attacks,</i>

00:26:51.900 --> 00:26:57.030
<i>suffered fractures and internal injuries</i>
<i>that would take a year to heal.</i>

00:26:57.360 --> 00:26:58.400
Gonta!

00:27:00.950 --> 00:27:04.990
<i>The news report plunged</i>
<i>the raccoons into depression.</i>

00:27:05.330 --> 00:27:09.120
<i>But when the news began to cover</i>
<i>the locals' fears of divine retribution,</i>

00:27:09.210 --> 00:27:12.290
<i>their spirits soared again.</i>

00:27:12.790 --> 00:27:17.460
<i>Maybe it was a mistake,</i>
<i>moving that Shinto shrine.</i>

00:27:17.960 --> 00:27:19.470
<i>What do you mean?</i>

00:27:19.550 --> 00:27:24.180
<i>Maybe all these incidents are revenge</i>
<i>from the gods of the shrine.</i>

00:27:24.550 --> 00:27:28.350
<i>It's true that a lot of Jizo statues</i>
<i>and shrines have been moved.</i>

00:27:28.480 --> 00:27:30.980
<i>Yes, that really worried me.</i>

00:27:31.060 --> 00:27:33.650
<i>I asked the developers to observe</i>
<i>the proper ceremonies</i>

00:27:33.730 --> 00:27:35.770
<i>before moving them, but...</i>

00:27:35.860 --> 00:27:38.230
<i>Professor Mizuki,</i>
<i>what do you think about all this?</i>

00:27:39.400 --> 00:27:44.450
<i>These spirits are usually associated</i>
<i>with a given location.</i>

00:27:45.280 --> 00:27:50.120
<i>If their abodes are moved,</i>
<i>they'll try to return home.</i>

00:27:50.210 --> 00:27:54.420
<i>If they do, and everything has changed,</i>
<i>they naturally become upset.</i>

00:27:54.500 --> 00:27:58.460
<i>I have a feeling</i>
<i>there's a lot more trouble to come.</i>

00:28:00.510 --> 00:28:02.720
Maybe I can save my woods after all.

00:28:06.680 --> 00:28:09.560
<i>Shokichi and the others went into action.</i>

00:28:16.610 --> 00:28:19.280
<i>The owner of Shokichi's woods</i>
<i>came to inspect his property</i>

00:28:19.400 --> 00:28:22.200
<i>with one of the developers</i>
<i>before construction began.</i>

00:28:22.280 --> 00:28:25.240
<i>To his surprise, he saw far more</i>
<i>Jizo statues than he remembered.</i>

00:28:25.320 --> 00:28:29.240
<i>"I'd better give this more thought,"</i>
<i>he told the developer,</i>

00:28:29.330 --> 00:28:31.700
<i>and he held off on signing</i>
<i>the contract to sell his land.</i>

00:28:32.620 --> 00:28:35.960
<i>During a ceremony at another shrine</i>
<i>that was slated to be moved,</i>

00:28:36.460 --> 00:28:43.300
<i>one of the raccoons suddenly appeared</i>
<i>on the roof disguised as a fox,</i>

00:28:43.430 --> 00:28:45.800
<i>the shrine's servant to the gods.</i>

00:28:47.970 --> 00:28:52.430
<i>The fox's eerie cry brought the</i>
<i>proceedings to an immediate halt.</i>

00:28:52.560 --> 00:28:55.940
<i>The ceremony was cancelled,</i>
<i>the shrine's relocation put on hold,</i>

00:28:56.020 --> 00:28:58.150
<i>and residents petitioned the authorities</i>

00:28:58.230 --> 00:29:01.230
<i>to change plans for a road</i>
<i>through the area.</i>

00:29:02.690 --> 00:29:04.990
<i>The raccoons were on a roll.</i>

00:29:14.710 --> 00:29:19.000
<i>Each group tried to outdo the others</i>

00:29:19.090 --> 00:29:21.590
<i>in a campaign of guerrilla operations.</i>

00:29:21.710 --> 00:29:24.220
<i>Come this way!</i>

00:29:25.930 --> 00:29:29.390
Go away!

00:29:32.100 --> 00:29:34.270
Take it with you!

00:29:37.440 --> 00:29:39.650
Let's take all the trash
and leftovers with us.

00:29:39.860 --> 00:29:41.440
The leftovers!

00:29:41.610 --> 00:29:44.110
Leave them behind!

00:29:49.450 --> 00:29:51.280
Is something wrong, miss?

00:29:56.750 --> 00:29:58.630
What's the trouble?

00:30:09.890 --> 00:30:11.140
I have no face!

00:30:13.640 --> 00:30:15.180
A specter!

00:30:47.720 --> 00:30:51.050
-J-j-just now, I... I saw--
-A murder?

00:30:51.300 --> 00:30:53.050
N-no, it was...

00:30:53.680 --> 00:30:55.770
Not a murder? Too bad!

00:30:56.520 --> 00:30:59.600
Th-th-there was a woman!

00:30:59.730 --> 00:31:04.150
-Did she have a mouth like a shark?
-No! No! She was... I mean...

00:31:04.270 --> 00:31:08.150
Then, was she something like this?

00:31:09.450 --> 00:31:10.910
It's her!

00:31:25.000 --> 00:31:31.590
Was... she... something... like... this?

00:31:39.230 --> 00:31:43.940
<i>The raccoons took endless delight</i>
<i>in frightening the humans.</i>

00:31:44.810 --> 00:31:47.940
<i>After every big success,</i>
<i>they held a celebration.</i>

00:31:51.320 --> 00:31:55.200
<i>But Gonta, the one who started it all,</i>

00:31:55.330 --> 00:31:58.410
<i>showed no signs of recovering</i>
<i>from his injuries.</i>

00:31:58.490 --> 00:32:00.960
<i>His loving wife Otama</i>
<i>cared for him tenderly,</i>

00:32:01.040 --> 00:32:04.420
<i>but she could not soothe his frustration</i>
<i>at being out of the fight.</i>

00:32:04.960 --> 00:32:08.250
<i>Frankly, Gonta thought</i>
<i>his raccoon friends were wimps.</i>

00:32:08.590 --> 00:32:11.260
Yesterday's <i>News Train</i> was priceless.

00:32:11.340 --> 00:32:13.930
You know that special
about "Tama New Specter Town"?

00:32:14.010 --> 00:32:16.890
They interviewed the cop we scared.

00:32:16.970 --> 00:32:22.770
The other guests laughed in his face.
He was so furious! I almost died!

00:32:22.890 --> 00:32:26.980
Idiot! So what?
Are they going to stop the project

00:32:27.110 --> 00:32:28.360
just because of stuff like that?

00:32:28.480 --> 00:32:30.690
If you're going to shape-shift,
do it the way I did!

00:32:31.280 --> 00:32:34.740
Cause accidents, and kill them!

00:32:34.820 --> 00:32:38.660
-Oh, no!
-Gonta!

00:32:39.120 --> 00:32:41.250
<i>It was just as Gonta said.</i>

00:32:41.500 --> 00:32:43.210
<i>The project didn't stop.</i>

00:32:43.620 --> 00:32:49.210
<i>Rivers were encased in concrete,</i>
<i>roads were laid out everywhere,</i>

00:32:49.300 --> 00:32:50.760
<i>masses of building material flowed in,</i>

00:32:51.130 --> 00:32:53.930
<i>and the construction of thousands of</i>
<i>apartments finally got under way.</i>

00:32:54.430 --> 00:32:58.050
<i>The strange happenings</i>
<i>on the construction sites</i>

00:32:58.180 --> 00:32:59.260
<i>and in the hills</i>

00:32:59.350 --> 00:33:04.560
<i>received nationwide coverage.</i>

00:33:04.810 --> 00:33:07.770
<i>The raccoons were gaining</i>
<i>confidence in their ultimate victory.</i>

00:33:10.070 --> 00:33:12.780
Rock, paper, scissors...

00:33:16.740 --> 00:33:18.780
<i>Autumn, year 32 of the Pom Poko era.</i>

00:33:19.410 --> 00:33:22.580
<i>It was time to choose messengers</i>
<i>to travel to Sade and Shikoku islands</i>

00:33:22.700 --> 00:33:24.910
<i>to seek help</i>
<i>from famous shape-shifting masters.</i>

00:33:26.370 --> 00:33:29.790
<i>Tamasaburo of Oni Woods</i>
<i>was chosen to go to Shikoku.</i>

00:33:30.630 --> 00:33:33.840
<i>Bunta of Mizunomi Marsh</i>
<i>was chosen to travel to Sado.</i>

00:33:36.840 --> 00:33:39.680
<i>So at the next full moon,</i>

00:33:39.760 --> 00:33:44.560
<i>the two young raccoons</i>
<i>said farewell to their comrades</i>

00:33:44.640 --> 00:33:47.850
<i>and set out for their destinations</i>
<i>in high spirits.</i>

00:34:01.740 --> 00:34:03.040
What a smell!

00:34:04.950 --> 00:34:10.330
<i>The raccoons continued</i>
<i>haunting the construction sites.</i>

00:34:17.050 --> 00:34:20.220
<i>They were having so much fun</i>
<i>with their shape-shifting,</i>

00:34:20.340 --> 00:34:24.470
<i>they almost didn't care</i>
<i>whether it was effective or not.</i>

00:34:39.450 --> 00:34:41.120
-Out with the demons!
-Daddy!

00:35:06.430 --> 00:35:10.270
Will this really drive out the humans?

00:35:11.900 --> 00:35:15.900
Won't they see through us
one of these days?

00:35:17.280 --> 00:35:20.740
Maybe we should really go after them,
like Gonta says.

00:35:22.070 --> 00:35:26.450
What does it matter
if one or two get killed?

00:35:28.160 --> 00:35:32.750
"To be or not to be,
that is the question."

00:35:43.470 --> 00:35:44.470
Kiyo!

00:35:48.680 --> 00:35:50.480
What are you doing up there?

00:35:55.150 --> 00:35:56.230
Something wrong with your neck?

00:35:58.110 --> 00:36:02.110
I was posing for you.
I was hoping you'd say I was pretty.

00:36:02.700 --> 00:36:03.610
Oh, sorry.

00:36:04.660 --> 00:36:06.620
Now there really is something wrong
with my neck.

00:36:07.290 --> 00:36:08.580
You looked pretty.

00:36:09.000 --> 00:36:09.830
It's too late.

00:36:10.450 --> 00:36:11.660
I mean it.

00:36:14.960 --> 00:36:17.460
It's okay. I just need more practice.

00:36:27.050 --> 00:36:30.180
<i>One day a raccoon from Potamochi Mountain</i>

00:36:31.020 --> 00:36:34.440
Everyone likes that song, don't they?
I kind of like it myself.

00:36:35.230 --> 00:36:37.150
Do you know the song,
"Where Are You From?"

00:36:37.270 --> 00:36:39.530
Yes, but I can't sing all the lyrics.

00:36:39.650 --> 00:36:40.740
That song used to be--

00:36:40.900 --> 00:36:46.950
<i>There was a raccoon from Senba</i>
<i>Along came a hunter</i>

00:36:47.410 --> 00:36:49.580
A hunter shot my grandpa.

00:36:51.500 --> 00:36:53.080
I'm sorry. I didn't know.

00:36:53.790 --> 00:36:58.790
That's okay.
But Grandpa wasn't boiled or fried.

00:36:59.050 --> 00:37:02.800
Someone paid a lot for his pelt.

00:37:03.720 --> 00:37:05.090
I really like your fur too.

00:37:05.640 --> 00:37:08.470
Why, that makes me happy.
Coming from you, that is.

00:37:12.600 --> 00:37:14.520
So, what were you going to say
about that song?

00:37:15.020 --> 00:37:18.900
My father used to sing it.

00:37:19.020 --> 00:37:20.520
He was a good ball-bouncer too.

00:37:20.650 --> 00:37:23.360
He must have been a character.

00:37:24.240 --> 00:37:29.450
Whenever he got to the end of the song,
he always warned us.

00:37:30.160 --> 00:37:31.330
About what?

00:37:31.450 --> 00:37:34.120
"You kids better remember:

00:37:34.620 --> 00:37:36.790
"Even in a simple ball-bouncing song,

00:37:36.870 --> 00:37:39.210
"you hear about the cruel nature
of humans."

00:37:39.290 --> 00:37:44.130
"How they hunt us raccoons, kill us
and eat us. And don't you forget it!"

00:37:48.390 --> 00:37:50.300
Say, shall we bounce balls?

00:37:50.760 --> 00:37:52.140
Are you good at it?

00:37:52.220 --> 00:37:53.770
Yes, I'm pretty good.

00:37:58.900 --> 00:38:00.690
Then I better do my best too!

00:38:06.570 --> 00:38:10.990
<i>Where are you from? Higo</i>
<i>Where's Higo?</i>

00:38:11.160 --> 00:38:15.750
<i>In Kumamoto</i>
<i>Where's Kumamoto? In Semba</i>

00:38:15.870 --> 00:38:19.630
<i>There was a raccoon from Semba</i>

00:38:19.750 --> 00:38:20.920
<i>Along came--</i>

00:38:21.000 --> 00:38:24.920
Shokichi, when are you going to do
that "Operation Twin Star" you mentioned?

00:38:25.010 --> 00:38:27.590
Oh, I don't really want to do it anymore.

00:38:27.720 --> 00:38:30.140
But it was such a good plan.

00:38:31.800 --> 00:38:33.850
Why don't we do it tonight?
Just the two of us.

00:38:34.220 --> 00:38:35.600
With you?

00:38:36.480 --> 00:38:37.980
Are you afraid to do it with me?

00:38:38.270 --> 00:38:41.480
No, it's not that. It's just...

00:38:42.020 --> 00:38:45.650
Then let's try.
I'm sure it will go over really well.

00:38:46.360 --> 00:38:50.280
Okay, let's do it! With you as my partner,
I bet things will go great.

00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:52.280
I can't wait!

00:39:03.090 --> 00:39:05.920
Well, well, what adorable little children!

00:39:06.880 --> 00:39:11.550
We just got back from a trip
to the stars, but our home is gone.

00:39:12.300 --> 00:39:13.550
A trip to the stars?

00:39:13.970 --> 00:39:19.020
From red-eyed Scorpio
to the Eagle's wings...

00:39:19.190 --> 00:39:23.690
From the coils of the Snake
to the brow of the Bear Cub!

00:39:24.480 --> 00:39:29.240
We sprinkle the dew and frost
as we fly among the stars.

00:39:29.320 --> 00:39:31.780
What is this?

00:39:34.780 --> 00:39:37.500
Our home is gone! We're cold!

00:39:37.830 --> 00:39:40.580
Mister, do you know where our home went?

00:39:41.670 --> 00:39:45.290
Your home? I don't know what you mean.

00:39:46.090 --> 00:39:48.800
Nobody knows! Run along now!

00:39:48.880 --> 00:39:51.340
We should call the police.
Someone get the police here!

00:39:56.930 --> 00:39:58.470
Hey, what are you kids doing?

00:40:12.070 --> 00:40:14.160
They're not kids, they're spirits!

00:40:14.280 --> 00:40:15.370
Spirits?

00:40:15.700 --> 00:40:19.250
Little spirits, please don't be angry!

00:40:40.600 --> 00:40:42.640
Now, just hold on a minute.

00:40:42.730 --> 00:40:46.190
I'll treat you right! You want a raise?
Come on, give me a break!

00:40:46.440 --> 00:40:53.110
No, I've had it. I'm going back home.
I can't stay in these haunted hills.

00:40:53.320 --> 00:40:55.910
Come on, Suzuki.

00:40:56.070 --> 00:41:01.200
I heard Tokyo was a scary place,
but this is too much for me.

00:41:01.290 --> 00:41:03.580
You'd better stop the construction.

00:41:03.660 --> 00:41:05.370
Whether it's gods or devils,

00:41:05.540 --> 00:41:07.960
somebody or something
is really upset about this project.

00:41:14.720 --> 00:41:17.390
<i>The raccoons cheered.</i>

00:41:17.890 --> 00:41:21.020
<i>That evening's celebrations</i>
<i>were especially grand.</i>

00:41:21.390 --> 00:41:26.060
<i>Naturally, the guests of honor</i>
<i>were the two heroes, Kiyo and Shokichi.</i>

00:41:31.110 --> 00:41:36.200
<i>Meanwhile, the workers' quarters</i>
<i>were dark and silent.</i>

00:41:37.110 --> 00:41:38.950
<i>But the next morning...</i>

00:41:41.330 --> 00:41:43.750
<i>It seemed there was</i>
<i>an endless supply of humans.</i>

00:41:44.250 --> 00:41:46.580
<i>No matter how many</i>
<i>the raccoons scared away,</i>

00:41:46.670 --> 00:41:49.880
<i>there were always others</i>
<i>to take their place.</i>

00:41:51.590 --> 00:41:53.380
It's rumored among local residents

00:41:53.510 --> 00:41:56.430
that this may be
the work of foxes and raccoons.

00:41:58.010 --> 00:41:59.970
That would make things simple enough.

00:42:00.050 --> 00:42:04.180
All we'd have to do is
exterminate all the offending animals.

00:42:04.560 --> 00:42:07.190
<i>The raccoons who were watching</i>
<i>were shocked.</i>

00:42:07.730 --> 00:42:12.570
<i>But these incidents</i>
<i>are right out of old folk tales.</i>

00:42:12.900 --> 00:42:15.570
<i>It's not surprising people think</i>
<i>foxes and raccoons are behind it.</i>

00:42:15.650 --> 00:42:20.200
<i>But that is precisely the proof</i>
<i>that this is all just malicious rumors.</i>

00:42:20.280 --> 00:42:23.200
<i>What do you mean, rumors?</i>
<i>I saw it with my own eyes!</i>

00:42:23.490 --> 00:42:24.700
<i>Oh, all right.</i>

00:42:25.700 --> 00:42:30.210
<i>In that case, we'll issue</i>
<i>an extermination order for these pests.</i>

00:42:30.790 --> 00:42:33.550
<i>As soon as you find</i>
<i>any more raccoons playing more tricks,</i>

00:42:33.670 --> 00:42:35.090
<i>let us know immediately.</i>

00:42:35.710 --> 00:42:38.430
<i>That is, if you can prove it!</i>

00:42:41.220 --> 00:42:44.060
<i>Shokichi was not the only one</i>
<i>who wondered</i>

00:42:44.140 --> 00:42:46.680
<i>whether shape-shifting was enough</i>
<i>to drive out the humans.</i>

00:42:46.810 --> 00:42:50.560
As you all know, the Edo period
was a golden age for raccoons.

00:42:50.850 --> 00:42:54.440
Raccoon shape-shifting was

00:42:54.530 --> 00:42:58.900
a frequent
subject for painters and writers.

00:42:59.360 --> 00:43:02.660
But unfortunately,
we raccoons were too conspicuous.

00:43:02.740 --> 00:43:04.910
We aroused the resentment of humans.

00:43:05.490 --> 00:43:10.870
In the modern era,
we've been hunted for our pelts,

00:43:10.960 --> 00:43:14.210
and our fur has been used
for paintbrushes and toothbrushes.

00:43:14.500 --> 00:43:17.920
That's how the humans
took revenge for our excesses.

00:43:18.880 --> 00:43:20.340
Don't any of you ever forget:

00:43:20.430 --> 00:43:23.470
the past few decades
have been peaceful for us raccoons

00:43:23.550 --> 00:43:26.100
only because we've exercised restraint

00:43:26.680 --> 00:43:32.860
and not used shape-shifting too often.

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:36.280
Our talents are a two-edged sword.

00:43:36.440 --> 00:43:39.570
I want all of you to use this technique
with discretion.

00:43:39.700 --> 00:43:45.370
Otherwise, we'll invite
further retribution from the humans.

00:43:48.750 --> 00:43:53.460
<i>Oroku's speech dashed cold water</i>
<i>on the spirits of the young raccoons.</i>

00:43:54.040 --> 00:43:57.500
<i>And now autumn was upon them,</i>

00:43:57.630 --> 00:44:00.720
<i>the time of year when raccoons</i>
<i>need enough food to store ample fat</i>

00:44:00.840 --> 00:44:05.220
<i>and grow the long, fluffy coats</i>
<i>needed for the coming winter.</i>

00:44:20.780 --> 00:44:24.950
<i>The young raccoons focused their</i>
<i>attention and shape-shifting skills</i>

00:44:25.030 --> 00:44:27.660
<i>on getting food for the winter.</i>

00:44:30.200 --> 00:44:36.130
<i>One day, an exhausted raccoon</i>
<i>arrived in Tama Hills.</i>

00:44:53.810 --> 00:44:55.730
Don't worry, we're raccoons too!

00:45:00.360 --> 00:45:01.740
Thank you very much.

00:45:03.280 --> 00:45:08.330
You seem completely worn out.
Where did you come from?

00:45:08.410 --> 00:45:09.910
From Fujino Woods.

00:45:10.040 --> 00:45:11.750
Is that on Shikoku island? Sado island?

00:45:12.120 --> 00:45:15.750
Why, no.
It's just over the mountains from here.

00:45:16.130 --> 00:45:20.630
Just over the mountains?
So you're not from Shikoku after all.

00:45:21.880 --> 00:45:26.090
Oh, my, I'm sorry.
I'm afraid I've disappointed you.

00:45:26.220 --> 00:45:29.300
No, it's just that we've been waiting
for someone from there.

00:45:29.510 --> 00:45:33.640
So, what brought you here?

00:45:34.060 --> 00:45:38.270
Now I finally know
where all that dirt is coming from,

00:45:38.360 --> 00:45:39.900
the dirt that's ruining our woods!

00:45:41.650 --> 00:45:43.990
<i>According to this raccoon named Hayashi,</i>

00:45:44.070 --> 00:45:49.530
<i>a huge amount of excavated dirt was</i>
<i>being illegally dumped in Fujino Woods.</i>

00:45:49.990 --> 00:45:53.040
<i>The streams were polluted,</i>
<i>there were frequent landslides,</i>

00:45:53.120 --> 00:45:57.540
<i>and the raccoons and other animals</i>
<i>of the woods were in dire straits.</i>

00:45:58.920 --> 00:46:02.670
<i>To find out where all this</i>
<i>discarded earth was coming from,</i>

00:46:02.750 --> 00:46:07.720
<i>Hayashi assumed human form and caught</i>
<i>a ride on one of the dump trucks.</i>

00:46:16.270 --> 00:46:17.230
<i>Unfortunately,</i>

00:46:17.520 --> 00:46:20.360
<i>shape-shifting</i>
<i>was not one of his strong points.</i>

00:46:20.440 --> 00:46:24.190
<i>The swaying of the truck and the stress</i>
<i>of the journey made him fall asleep,</i>

00:46:24.280 --> 00:46:26.530
<i>and he changed back into a raccoon.</i>

00:46:26.990 --> 00:46:30.240
It's not just Fujino Woods.
Other woods are being ruined too.

00:46:30.320 --> 00:46:34.160
And now there are garbage dumps
and golf courses all over the place.

00:46:34.910 --> 00:46:38.040
Our Tama Hills are levelled,
and we suffer.

00:46:38.620 --> 00:46:43.250
Then the dirt is dumped in Fujino Woods,
and you suffer.

00:46:43.670 --> 00:46:45.800
When will this insanity end?

00:46:47.760 --> 00:46:51.050
And I was so astonished
at what I found here!

00:46:51.140 --> 00:46:55.810
I thought the trucks came
from some site in the middle of Tokyo.

00:46:56.270 --> 00:46:58.350
But we're in the hills here!

00:46:58.440 --> 00:47:00.940
They dig up one hill
and dump it on another!

00:47:01.020 --> 00:47:04.940
I just can't understand
why the humans are doing this.

00:47:05.940 --> 00:47:09.450
So if we stop the construction,

00:47:09.530 --> 00:47:12.820
it will help the raccoons
in Fujino Woods too, right?

00:47:14.030 --> 00:47:16.910
What stirring words!

00:47:17.290 --> 00:47:19.710
I beg you all to use
your skills in shape-shifting

00:47:20.540 --> 00:47:25.590
to save our woods too!

00:47:25.710 --> 00:47:31.130
Well, you see,
it's not really that simple, even for us.

00:47:35.470 --> 00:47:39.310
Where could Bunta and Tamasaburo be?

00:47:39.390 --> 00:47:42.730
They were supposed to go
and fetch the masters to help us.

00:47:46.070 --> 00:47:50.820
<i>There was no word from Shikoku or Sade.</i>

00:47:50.900 --> 00:47:53.160
<i>And so winter came to Tama Hills.</i>

00:47:54.320 --> 00:47:56.830
<i>With the raccoons down for the winter,</i>

00:47:56.910 --> 00:47:59.830
<i>the haunting of Tama New Town</i>
<i>was forgotten,</i>

00:48:00.080 --> 00:48:02.670
<i>and media attention evaporated.</i>

00:48:02.870 --> 00:48:05.670
<i>The papers were filled with stories</i>
<i>about celebrity scandals</i>

00:48:05.790 --> 00:48:08.630
<i>and sordid political goings-on.</i>

00:48:14.050 --> 00:48:17.390
<i>Sleet covers the garden of Manpuku Temple</i>

00:48:17.510 --> 00:48:21.310
<i>The sleet's like ice cream</i>

00:48:21.390 --> 00:48:25.940
<i>All our friends are here</i>
<i>Pom Poko pun pun, pun pun</i>

00:48:26.860 --> 00:48:29.070
<i>New Year's Day,</i>
<i>year 33 of the Pom Poko era.</i>

00:48:29.690 --> 00:48:33.660
<i>Tama Hills greeted the new year</i>
<i>under a rare blanket of snow.</i>

00:48:35.410 --> 00:48:39.790
<i>Most of the construction workers</i>
<i>had already returned to their hometowns</i>

00:48:39.870 --> 00:48:45.080
<i>and were enjoying the holidays</i>
<i>surrounded by their families.</i>

00:48:45.250 --> 00:48:50.510
Push! Push! Push!

00:49:00.600 --> 00:49:02.600
<i>Our golden balls swing and swing</i>

00:49:02.730 --> 00:49:06.520
<i>Though there's not a breath of wind</i>

00:49:06.810 --> 00:49:10.820
<i>The baby raccoon sees our balls</i>

00:49:10.900 --> 00:49:14.530
<i>And swings his--</i>

00:49:14.860 --> 00:49:16.660
We saw it! It really happened!

00:49:16.820 --> 00:49:19.370
<i>A bunch of raccoons pushed</i>
<i>that bulldozer over the cliff!</i>

00:49:19.450 --> 00:49:20.540
We're not lying!

00:49:21.120 --> 00:49:24.620
<i>Police suspect the workers, who stayed</i>
<i>behind over the new year holidays,</i>

00:49:24.710 --> 00:49:29.800
<i>were inspired by the numerous pranks</i>
<i>that finally stopped last autumn.</i>

00:49:29.960 --> 00:49:31.550
<i>However, snow</i>
<i>around the crime scene has melted,</i>

00:49:32.050 --> 00:49:34.420
<i>and it may be difficult</i>
<i>to gather evidence.</i>

00:49:34.510 --> 00:49:36.550
I hope you know what you're doing,
Shokichi.

00:49:37.010 --> 00:49:39.220
Oh, I think we'll be all right.

00:49:39.300 --> 00:49:41.390
What a stupid prank.

00:49:41.520 --> 00:49:42.350
Not at all.

00:49:42.720 --> 00:49:46.230
Shokichi was trying to encourage
the raccoons who can't shape-shift

00:49:46.350 --> 00:49:47.520
by giving them a way to help.

00:49:47.600 --> 00:49:49.520
What do you think, Osho?

00:49:49.610 --> 00:49:53.320
Hmm, I don't see any great harm done.

00:49:53.650 --> 00:49:55.820
<i>It was just as Osho predicted.</i>

00:49:56.320 --> 00:49:59.780
The three workers were released
for lack of evidence.

00:49:59.870 --> 00:50:02.950
<i>Naturally, no one believed the raccoons</i>
<i>were responsible.</i>

00:50:03.040 --> 00:50:04.830
<i>The case remained unsolved.</i>

00:50:14.880 --> 00:50:16.630
<i>And so spring came.</i>

00:50:19.930 --> 00:50:21.890
<i>The season of love had arrived once again</i>

00:50:22.850 --> 00:50:25.680
<i>The raccoons had been chaste</i>
<i>for more than a year,</i>

00:50:25.770 --> 00:50:27.560
<i>and couldn't control themselves</i>
<i>any longer.</i>

00:50:28.730 --> 00:50:33.150
<i>The air was filled with sweet nothings,</i>
<i>and the raccoons pursued</i>

00:50:33.360 --> 00:50:36.190
<i>and wooed each other</i>
<i>until the very skies turned rosy.</i>

00:50:41.030 --> 00:50:42.280
Hanako! Wait!

00:50:49.500 --> 00:50:50.460
Hanako!

00:50:51.000 --> 00:50:53.380
You're walking much better!

00:50:55.590 --> 00:50:58.130
Hanako! Wait just a minute!

00:50:58.720 --> 00:51:00.720
Can't you catch me?

00:51:03.680 --> 00:51:05.600
Everyone has spring fever.

00:51:06.060 --> 00:51:08.640
I guess we're all
like the flowers and the trees.

00:51:09.440 --> 00:51:12.060
When winter ends
and the sun shines down on us,

00:51:12.150 --> 00:51:13.940
we can't help sending out shoots.

00:51:14.480 --> 00:51:17.940
Then at last we blossom and bear fruit.

00:51:20.110 --> 00:51:23.660
But we have to keep our promise to Granny.

00:51:24.660 --> 00:51:28.000
Let's stay chaste
until we've finally won this war.

00:51:28.580 --> 00:51:33.170
Shokichi, you're so wonderful.

00:51:33.670 --> 00:51:35.670
I'm so happy!

00:51:38.130 --> 00:51:40.470
Our love will last forever!

00:51:42.890 --> 00:51:43.720
Shokichi!

00:51:51.730 --> 00:51:53.100
<i>That was a mistake.</i>

00:51:53.690 --> 00:51:55.360
<i>Their love grew passionate,</i>

00:51:55.820 --> 00:51:57.690
<i>and later that year,</i>

00:51:57.780 --> 00:52:03.700
<i>four charming young raccoons</i>
<i>were born to Kiyo and Shokichi.</i>

00:53:02.380 --> 00:53:04.220
KINCHO DAIMYO SHRINE

00:53:04.340 --> 00:53:05.890
<i>Now, the previous autumn,</i>

00:53:06.390 --> 00:53:09.140
<i>Tamasaburo had managed to reach</i>
<i>the island of Shikoku</i>

00:53:09.600 --> 00:53:13.100
<i>after many trials and hardships.</i>

00:53:13.180 --> 00:53:17.150
<i>He presented his request for help</i>
<i>to the shape-shifting master Kincho VI,</i>

00:53:17.230 --> 00:53:19.900
<i>but then he collapsed</i>
<i>and was very ill for many weeks.</i>

00:53:19.980 --> 00:53:23.820
<i>Luckily, Kincho had a daughter, Koharu,</i>
<i>who stayed by Tamasaburo's bedside</i>

00:53:23.900 --> 00:53:25.780
<i>and miraculously</i>
<i>nursed him back to health.</i>

00:53:25.860 --> 00:53:28.160
<i>With the coming of spring,</i>
<i>their bond deepened,</i>

00:53:28.490 --> 00:53:31.330
<i>and Koharu bore Tamasaburo three cubs.</i>

00:53:36.000 --> 00:53:41.920
<i>The island's elders held a council</i>
<i>in the inner chambers of the shrine.</i>

00:53:42.590 --> 00:53:45.430
<i>They all agreed that stopping</i>
<i>Tama New Town's development</i>

00:53:45.510 --> 00:53:51.060
<i>would send a message</i>
<i>to similar development projects</i>

00:53:51.140 --> 00:53:53.730
<i>all over Japan.</i>

00:53:54.180 --> 00:53:56.690
<i>But the elders were divided</i>
<i>as to who to send,</i>

00:53:56.770 --> 00:53:58.690
<i>how affairs in Shikoku would be handled,</i>

00:53:59.270 --> 00:54:01.650
<i>and how to avoid any succession disputes</i>
<i>that might arise</i>

00:54:01.730 --> 00:54:04.690
<i>in case something should happen</i>
<i>to one of the participants.</i>

00:54:04.780 --> 00:54:08.200
<i>Hundreds of questions were raised,</i>
<i>but no conclusions were reached.</i>

00:54:09.120 --> 00:54:15.000
It's such beautiful weather. But Father
and the others just talk, talk, talk.

00:54:15.710 --> 00:54:19.080
They've been debating for six months now.

00:54:19.670 --> 00:54:22.630
When will they ever reach a decision?

00:54:24.130 --> 00:54:27.090
Oh, I hope they never reach a decision!

00:54:31.640 --> 00:54:34.770
Tamasaburo, just the thought
that you might someday return

00:54:34.850 --> 00:54:41.820
to far-off Tama Hills
makes my heart ache with sadness.

00:54:45.820 --> 00:54:52.120
Koharu... I too dream
that our happiness never ends.

00:54:52.780 --> 00:54:54.790
Why must it be just a dream?

00:54:57.120 --> 00:55:01.000
I'll ask Father.

00:55:01.080 --> 00:55:05.510
I'll ask him to let you stay here
and be his successor.

00:55:18.890 --> 00:55:22.900
<i>While Tamasaburo was struggling</i>
<i>to make a decision,</i>

00:55:23.060 --> 00:55:28.400
<i>Bunta of Mizunomi Marsh roamed</i>
<i>the fields and mountains of Sade island,</i>

00:55:28.610 --> 00:55:30.450
<i>searching for Danzaburo,</i>

00:55:30.530 --> 00:55:32.740
<i>a shape-shifting master.</i>

00:55:33.030 --> 00:55:39.830
<i>But he couldn't find anyone who knew</i>
<i>anything about the master's whereabouts.</i>

00:55:46.710 --> 00:55:48.510
<i>During the summer and autumn of that year,</i>

00:55:48.590 --> 00:55:51.510
<i>the raccoons of Tama Hills</i>
<i>were beset by a series of misfortunes.</i>

00:55:51.930 --> 00:55:55.390
<i>Their woods continued to shrink</i>
<i>before the onslaught of development.</i>

00:55:55.470 --> 00:55:59.730
<i>And just when the baby boom of spring</i>
<i>had brought many new mouths to feed,</i>

00:56:00.100 --> 00:56:04.980
<i>poor summer weather</i>
<i>created a serious food shortage.</i>

00:56:05.070 --> 00:56:09.320
<i>There were not nearly enough chestnuts</i>
<i>and persimmons to eat that autumn.</i>

00:56:09.530 --> 00:56:11.450
<i>Those with shape-shifting skills</i>
<i>tried to help</i>

00:56:11.530 --> 00:56:14.200
<i>by gathering food meant for humans,</i>

00:56:14.280 --> 00:56:17.490
<i>but it was still not nearly enough</i>
<i>to feed the growing cubs.</i>

00:56:30.090 --> 00:56:32.260
<i>Finally, even raccoons</i>
<i>who could not shape-shift</i>

00:56:32.380 --> 00:56:35.640
<i>were forced to come out of the woods</i>
<i>and scavenge around human homes,</i>

00:56:35.720 --> 00:56:38.390
<i>looking for anything</i>
<i>to feed their children.</i>

00:56:38.640 --> 00:56:42.390
<i>Inevitably, some of them</i>
<i>began to lose their lives</i>

00:56:42.480 --> 00:56:47.360
<i>on the roads and in traps.</i>

00:57:24.190 --> 00:57:25.310
I can't take any more!

00:57:25.850 --> 00:57:29.770
The time has come for each of us
to take at least one human life,

00:57:29.860 --> 00:57:31.030
even if we lose our own.

00:57:31.110 --> 00:57:34.070
Are you sure you're all right now, Gonta?

00:57:34.150 --> 00:57:37.200
Of course! See? I'm in the pink!

00:57:46.080 --> 00:57:50.170
This is wonderful.
When should we celebrate your recovery?

00:57:51.340 --> 00:57:54.880
This isn't the time for parties, Granny.

00:57:55.720 --> 00:57:59.010
I think we should wait for the masters
of shape-shifting to get here

00:57:59.100 --> 00:58:01.310
before we decide our strategy.

00:58:01.390 --> 00:58:05.140
You too, Shokichi?
You're too young to be such a coward.

00:58:05.440 --> 00:58:07.900
You're wrong.
We can't underestimate the humans.

00:58:08.230 --> 00:58:11.190
If we attack them head on,
they'll destroy us.

00:58:12.150 --> 00:58:14.110
We've waited long enough!

00:58:14.190 --> 00:58:17.610
Be patient. Let's hear Shokichi out.

00:58:18.570 --> 00:58:22.240
I propose we adopt three policies
until the masters arrive.

00:58:22.330 --> 00:58:26.870
One: establish a system to hand out
food to raccoons who can't shape-shift.

00:58:27.120 --> 00:58:29.130
In other words, a rationing system.

00:58:30.630 --> 00:58:33.670
Two: thorough training in traffic safety.

00:58:35.010 --> 00:58:39.640
Three: the creation of rescue squads
for raccoons caught in traps.

00:58:39.800 --> 00:58:41.010
That's my proposal.

00:58:42.680 --> 00:58:46.850
Shokichi, you're practically
like one of the humans.

00:58:47.390 --> 00:58:50.100
No! I'm a raccoon, born and bred.

00:58:51.690 --> 00:58:57.240
Well then, leaving the particulars
to later. All in favor?

00:58:58.150 --> 00:58:59.450
Hands up!

00:58:59.910 --> 00:59:01.070
In favor!

00:59:03.280 --> 00:59:05.040
What is this nonsense, Gonta?

00:59:05.120 --> 00:59:07.080
It's not nonsense! It's a coup d'état!

00:59:07.830 --> 00:59:11.830
Anyone who opposes me from now on
will be killed by my private guard!

00:59:11.920 --> 00:59:14.170
-Got it?
-Yeah!

00:59:14.800 --> 00:59:17.420
Those are dangerous words, Gonta.

00:59:17.510 --> 00:59:20.090
That's "Sir Gon."

00:59:20.890 --> 00:59:24.220
Raccoons!
We all know the humans are dangerous.

00:59:24.310 --> 00:59:27.350
If we attack without concern
for our own safety, victory will be ours.

00:59:27.600 --> 00:59:32.650
They can be killed. As the saying goes,
"a trapped mouse will beat the cat."

00:59:33.310 --> 00:59:35.650
What's that supposed to mean?

00:59:35.730 --> 00:59:37.240
He doesn't look like a mouse.

00:59:37.320 --> 00:59:39.650
He means we can win if we're desperate.

00:59:39.740 --> 00:59:44.660
Exactly. If a mouse is cornered,
it'll find the strength to beat the cat.

00:59:45.410 --> 00:59:47.290
We're not mice, Gonta.

00:59:47.370 --> 00:59:49.410
What's the point in beating a cat?

00:59:49.910 --> 00:59:54.920
Come to think of it, it's been a while
since I had a nice mouse.

00:59:55.000 --> 00:59:56.800
Mouse tempura can't be beat.

00:59:57.260 --> 00:59:59.880
No, deep fried is the tastiest!

01:00:00.760 --> 01:00:03.800
Are you sure? I think the tempura batter
really makes it work.

01:00:04.300 --> 01:00:07.140
That crispy deep-fried tail!

01:00:09.520 --> 01:00:12.690
What the hell are you talking about!?

01:00:12.900 --> 01:00:18.480
What's important is
I love mouse tempura! Yes, I do!

01:00:18.990 --> 01:00:22.240
See Gonta? All we can think about is food.

01:00:23.570 --> 01:00:27.120
I think we'd better wait for the masters
to get here.

01:00:29.160 --> 01:00:30.620
My apologies.

01:00:30.830 --> 01:00:33.370
I suppose it was too much

01:00:34.380 --> 01:00:38.250
to expect the young raccoons
to stay chaste and not have babies.

01:00:38.670 --> 01:00:39.670
No!

01:00:40.340 --> 01:00:44.090
Instead of fewer raccoons,
we need fewer humans!

01:00:44.680 --> 01:00:48.810
The places they've infested
used to be our homes!

01:00:49.220 --> 01:00:53.020
The humans are the intruders!
Drive them out!

01:00:53.350 --> 01:00:54.600
Kill them!

01:00:55.150 --> 01:00:59.150
Drive them out! Kill them!

01:01:00.070 --> 01:01:01.360
<i>But at that very moment...</i>

01:01:16.880 --> 01:01:18.380
Hey, taxi!

01:01:50.410 --> 01:01:52.290
I'll tell everyone you're here!

01:02:03.880 --> 01:02:05.340
Tamasaburo!

01:02:06.010 --> 01:02:07.840
I've brought the masters from Shikoku!

01:02:11.640 --> 01:02:13.350
Tamasaburo! You did it!

01:02:22.940 --> 01:02:28.490
Friends, on our way here,
we saw your devastated woods.

01:02:28.950 --> 01:02:30.580
You have our deepest sympathy.

01:02:31.120 --> 01:02:36.080
We'd like to address all raccoons
tonight. There's no time to lose.

01:02:36.750 --> 01:02:39.130
<i>Year 33 of the Pom Poko era, autumn.</i>

01:02:39.210 --> 01:02:43.420
<i>All the raccoons assembled to welcome</i>
<i>the three masters from Shikoku.</i>

01:02:45.720 --> 01:02:49.640
There's a good moon out tonight.

01:02:50.180 --> 01:02:55.220
Fellow raccoons,
I am Tazaburo Hage of Yashima.

01:02:55.890 --> 01:03:00.480
I am 999 years old.

01:03:01.860 --> 01:03:08.700
Why is Honshu ravaged by development,
while Shikoku is almost untouched?

01:03:09.030 --> 01:03:13.990
The reason is, we raccoons
protect our woods vigilantly.

01:03:14.790 --> 01:03:18.000
The humans of Shikoku know

01:03:18.080 --> 01:03:23.920
that disaster will befall them
if they anger us.

01:03:24.420 --> 01:03:28.050
In fact, all three of us are worshipped

01:03:28.130 --> 01:03:33.600
at every shrine and temple in Shikoku.

01:03:33.890 --> 01:03:36.520
The humans revere us.

01:03:37.810 --> 01:03:39.480
But I have not introduced myself.

01:03:39.560 --> 01:03:42.730
I am lnugami Gyobu,

01:03:42.810 --> 01:03:46.860
supreme leader
of the raccoons of Matsuyama.

01:03:49.950 --> 01:03:54.700
I am Kincho VI, direct descendent
of Kincho Shrine's first raccoon master.

01:03:55.490 --> 01:03:59.000
To frighten the humans of Tokyo
and drive them out,

01:03:59.080 --> 01:04:03.000
we have resolved to carry out
Operation Specter.

01:04:03.840 --> 01:04:06.130
This operation will require

01:04:06.590 --> 01:04:10.420
unprecedented powers
of mental concentration,

01:04:10.510 --> 01:04:15.010
concentration so great
that the three of us may lose our lives.

01:04:16.600 --> 01:04:21.390
But if you successfully
carry out this plan,

01:04:21.850 --> 01:04:25.270
you will regain the humans' fear

01:04:25.360 --> 01:04:30.150
and respect without fail.

01:04:32.150 --> 01:04:37.330
And then, you can use
the humans' fear of raccoons

01:04:37.410 --> 01:04:42.460
to put an end to this infernal development
once and for all!

01:04:43.120 --> 01:04:45.590
We have a full array of potent tricks.

01:04:45.670 --> 01:04:49.460
We have brought you a boat, O raccoons,

01:04:49.550 --> 01:04:53.180
that will ferry all of you
back to a lost era of greatness!

01:04:53.430 --> 01:04:58.390
We promise you: all who come aboard
will reach those blessed shores!

01:05:10.690 --> 01:05:16.780
Hooray! Hooray!

01:05:17.490 --> 01:05:20.240
What a beautiful moon.

01:05:21.250 --> 01:05:24.040
We raccoons love moonlit nights.

01:05:24.580 --> 01:05:30.590
Let us pray to the moon
for the success of our enterprise.

01:05:30.800 --> 01:05:33.380
Right, everybody?

01:05:46.020 --> 01:05:50.980
<i>The raccoons immediately embarked</i>
<i>on a special regimen of training.</i>

01:06:06.290 --> 01:06:12.880
Congratulations on your
nine hundred and ninety-ninth birthday!

01:06:15.050 --> 01:06:19.350
Thank you everyone! Thank you!

01:06:20.600 --> 01:06:23.020
Master, please re-enact
the story of Yoichi the Archer,

01:06:23.100 --> 01:06:24.640
as you witnessed it in your younger days!

01:06:25.690 --> 01:06:27.560
So I shall!

01:07:13.770 --> 01:07:16.320
The time is ripe!

01:07:23.700 --> 01:07:26.200
Cock-a-doodle-doo!

01:07:30.880 --> 01:07:32.790
<i>Year 33 of the Pom Poko era, December.</i>

01:07:33.130 --> 01:07:36.300
<i>The day for Operation Specter</i>
<i>arrived at last.</i>

01:07:37.210 --> 01:07:41.430
<i>Slightly cloudy, no wind.</i>
<i>Thirteen degrees centigrade, humidity 65%.</i>

01:07:41.550 --> 01:07:43.760
<i>Perfect conditions for specters.</i>

01:08:19.800 --> 01:08:25.180
<i>Transformation into monsters and specters</i>
<i>has always been a raccoon strong point.</i>

01:08:25.350 --> 01:08:29.430
<i>But now, they needed to draw</i>
<i>not only on their own latent energy,</i>

01:08:29.850 --> 01:08:32.310
<i>but also the hidden energy of the cosmos:</i>

01:08:32.390 --> 01:08:37.900
<i>Fire, earth, water and air.</i>

01:08:37.980 --> 01:08:41.990
<i>The intensity of the training</i>
<i>undertaken by the raccoons</i>

01:08:43.240 --> 01:08:47.660
<i>under the tutelage</i>
<i>of the three elders of Shikoku</i>

01:08:48.620 --> 01:08:51.080
<i>is almost beyond description.</i>

01:08:51.580 --> 01:08:55.080
<i>All the raccoons,</i>
<i>even those who could not shape-shift,</i>

01:08:55.170 --> 01:08:58.500
<i>worked together</i>
<i>to focus their combined powers.</i>

01:09:01.590 --> 01:09:04.760
<i>That night, the fighting spirit</i>
<i>of the raccoons merged</i>

01:09:04.890 --> 01:09:06.430
<i>into one consuming flame.</i>

01:09:06.510 --> 01:09:10.140
<i>Their enthusiasm was so boundless,</i>
<i>they transformed themselves into specters</i>

01:09:10.220 --> 01:09:13.560
<i>long before they even reached</i>
<i>the dwellings of the humans.</i>

01:09:17.980 --> 01:09:19.530
Hey, look at that!

01:09:24.660 --> 01:09:25.870
What is it?

01:09:30.490 --> 01:09:35.210
Let the trees burst into full flower!

01:09:41.340 --> 01:09:46.300
Let the trees burst into full flower!

01:12:09.700 --> 01:12:12.450
Wow... it's a big parade of specters!

01:12:12.870 --> 01:12:16.870
I used to see stuff like that too,
way back when.

01:12:16.990 --> 01:12:20.460
You know, foxes with lanterns,
that kind of thing.

01:12:21.250 --> 01:12:24.340
You can really see them.

01:12:25.130 --> 01:12:27.210
You can see the lanterns.

01:12:27.760 --> 01:12:29.670
With little lights in them.

01:12:29.970 --> 01:12:34.600
You can see them marching along.

01:12:40.270 --> 01:12:43.440
I wonder why I could see them?

01:12:44.060 --> 01:12:46.980
Maybe foxes can really do that.

01:12:47.110 --> 01:12:49.690
I wonder.

01:12:53.450 --> 01:12:56.120
You can really see them.

01:12:56.330 --> 01:13:00.910
It must be your brain
playing tricks on you.

01:13:01.210 --> 01:13:07.420
A fox wedding. Foxes with lanterns.
It's already in your head.

01:13:07.500 --> 01:13:09.920
So, it's like...

01:13:10.960 --> 01:13:13.930
Your brain plays tricks on you.

01:13:14.010 --> 01:13:18.430
You can see them walking.
It's all in your head.

01:13:21.310 --> 01:13:26.730
Yeah, you're right.
There's no way it's real.

01:13:27.270 --> 01:13:30.780
People's brains are scary.

01:13:31.820 --> 01:13:34.570
You think things, and then you see them.

01:13:35.280 --> 01:13:38.160
There's no way they could be real, though.

01:13:41.160 --> 01:13:43.370
They really are real!

01:13:45.250 --> 01:13:48.380
It's just your brain
playing tricks on you.

01:13:53.220 --> 01:13:54.340
Welcome home.

01:13:56.970 --> 01:13:58.220
Sachiko!

01:14:12.730 --> 01:14:15.110
WAYS OF A PERVERT

01:14:17.490 --> 01:14:20.030
PUBLIC RESTROOM

01:14:45.980 --> 01:14:48.400
Matter is void!

01:14:56.950 --> 01:14:59.570
Form is emptiness!

01:15:34.150 --> 01:15:34.980
Here they come again!

01:16:14.730 --> 01:16:15.900
Master Gyobu!

01:16:17.030 --> 01:16:18.900
-Master Gyobu!
-Master Gyobu!

01:16:26.910 --> 01:16:28.290
That was amazing!

01:16:28.410 --> 01:16:30.120
That was scary, wasn't it?

01:16:32.250 --> 01:16:35.170
Aw, is that the end?

01:16:35.790 --> 01:16:38.550
-That was really cool!
-Yes.

01:16:38.800 --> 01:16:41.220
Come on, time for bed.

01:16:41.880 --> 01:16:43.010
Oh, okay...

01:16:45.890 --> 01:16:48.430
Don't forget to brush your teeth!

01:16:52.020 --> 01:16:54.440
I feel like I just woke up from a dream.

01:16:54.900 --> 01:16:57.940
Me too. What was all that about, I wonder?

01:16:59.070 --> 01:17:02.030
After that, flying saucers
would seem pretty tame.

01:17:02.610 --> 01:17:04.740
There are some things
you just can't explain.

01:17:09.870 --> 01:17:12.540
Long ago, when the Matsuyama
clan was at war,

01:17:12.620 --> 01:17:15.670
Gyobu went over to the enemy,
causing the downfall of his clan.

01:17:15.790 --> 01:17:19.460
He regretted this so deeply

01:17:19.840 --> 01:17:26.550
that he made a solemn vow to devote
his life to fighting for justice.

01:17:26.930 --> 01:17:30.600
We must ensure his sacrifice
was not in vain,

01:17:30.680 --> 01:17:37.230
emulate his noble spirit, and vow
not to rest until the day of our victory!

01:17:37.310 --> 01:17:41.570
<i>Gyahte gyahte hara gyahte</i>

01:17:41.650 --> 01:17:47.530
<i>A raccoon of Potamochi Mountain</i>

01:17:47.620 --> 01:17:51.120
<i>Got drunk and transformed himself</i>

01:17:51.450 --> 01:17:54.580
<i>Great success to Operation Specter</i>

01:17:54.710 --> 01:17:57.750
<i>The raccoons were so convinced</i>
<i>they had won</i>

01:17:58.000 --> 01:18:00.880
<i>that no one bothered</i>
<i>to watch the news on TV.</i>

01:18:01.550 --> 01:18:03.670
<i>Police and the media</i>
<i>are searching for anyone</i>

01:18:03.760 --> 01:18:06.840
<i>who might have videotaped</i>
<i>tonight's mysterious parade.</i>

01:18:06.930 --> 01:18:09.350
<i>But so far no one has come forward,</i>

01:18:09.430 --> 01:18:12.310
<i>complicating efforts</i>
<i>to determine what really happened.</i>

01:18:12.890 --> 01:18:17.060
<i>I'm sure I was taping the whole thing,</i>
<i>but there's nothing on the tape.</i>

01:18:17.600 --> 01:18:19.730
<i>It doesn't make any sense.</i>

01:18:19.820 --> 01:18:23.530
<i>The specter slipped in</i>
<i>right through this opening.</i>

01:18:23.690 --> 01:18:28.660
<i>It was terrifying!</i>
<i>Nobody could have staged that.</i>

01:18:29.620 --> 01:18:32.870
<i>There really is something strange</i>
<i>about New Town after all.</i>

01:18:33.370 --> 01:18:35.960
<i>I'd like to move out, but it's not easy.</i>

01:18:36.620 --> 01:18:38.880
<i>There will be a special program</i>
<i>at 12:20 am.</i>

01:18:38.960 --> 01:18:43.170
<i>With in-depth coverage</i>
<i>of this evening's strange events.</i>

01:18:53.930 --> 01:18:56.890
The more people investigate this,

01:18:57.390 --> 01:19:02.110
the more they will be convinced
it was no hallucination,

01:19:02.190 --> 01:19:05.740
that it all really happened!

01:19:06.150 --> 01:19:10.410
Then, when they realise
their science and logic are powerless

01:19:10.490 --> 01:19:14.290
to unlock the riddle of what happened...

01:19:14.370 --> 01:19:19.620
They'll be dumbfounded
by the awesome mystery of the cosmos,

01:19:20.210 --> 01:19:25.630
and realise how insignificant
human existence really is.

01:19:26.050 --> 01:19:30.470
Listen, everyone: Our good fortune
awaits, but let's not wait for it!

01:19:30.720 --> 01:19:32.930
Come then!

01:19:33.050 --> 01:19:38.690
Drink! Sing! Dance!

01:19:38.770 --> 01:19:43.150
Let's hear it for Master Hage!

01:19:44.360 --> 01:19:50.110
<i>But the next day,</i>
<i>events took a totally unexpected turn.</i>

01:19:50.820 --> 01:19:53.410
<i>It appears that the massive parade</i>
<i>staged yesterday</i>

01:19:53.580 --> 01:19:55.580
<i>in a residential complex of Tama New Town</i>

01:19:55.660 --> 01:19:57.950
<i>may have been</i>
<i>a publicity stunt for Wonderland,</i>

01:19:58.040 --> 01:20:00.000
<i>a theme park</i>
<i>now under construction in the area.</i>

01:20:00.080 --> 01:20:03.630
<i>Police have summoned PR executives</i>
<i>of Wonderland for questioning,</i>

01:20:03.710 --> 01:20:06.210
<i>on suspicion of having staged</i>
<i>a parade without a permit.</i>

01:20:06.460 --> 01:20:07.550
You gotta be kidding!

01:20:07.630 --> 01:20:10.180
<i>However, residents of the complex</i>
<i>and the surrounding area</i>

01:20:10.760 --> 01:20:12.510
<i>remain convinced</i>
<i>that what they saw yesterday</i>

01:20:12.640 --> 01:20:14.180
<i>could not have been a publicity stunt.</i>

01:20:14.550 --> 01:20:16.260
You can say that again!

01:20:16.680 --> 01:20:19.980
<i>The president of the company responsible</i>
<i>for Wonderland has admitted</i>

01:20:20.060 --> 01:20:21.980
<i>that the parade was a promotional event.</i>

01:20:22.400 --> 01:20:23.480
What?

01:20:24.150 --> 01:20:25.940
PRESIDENT OF WONDERLAND
AT EMERGENCY PRESS CONFERENCE

01:20:26.020 --> 01:20:32.820
<i>I deeply apologise for any inconvenience</i>
<i>caused by our parade yesterday.</i>

01:20:33.280 --> 01:20:34.490
Who the hell is he?

01:20:34.570 --> 01:20:40.160
<i>We just wanted the world</i>
<i>to know how wonderful, ah,</i>

01:20:41.250 --> 01:20:45.590
<i>Wonderland will be.</i>

01:20:45.670 --> 01:20:49.340
<i>So we decided the best way was to go out</i>
<i>and give the public a free taste of the...</i>

01:20:49.420 --> 01:20:52.840
<i>hmm, wonders they will soon be able</i>
<i>to experience in Wonderland.</i>

01:20:52.930 --> 01:20:57.140
<i>As president of Wonderland,</i>

01:20:57.220 --> 01:21:01.640
<i>I take full responsibility for the staging</i>
<i>of this unauthorized event.</i>

01:21:02.270 --> 01:21:03.940
-What a liar!
-That's ridiculous!

01:21:04.060 --> 01:21:05.110
<i>Fortunately,</i>

01:21:05.230 --> 01:21:09.690
<i>we received</i>
<i>an overwhelmingly positive response</i>

01:21:09.860 --> 01:21:14.070
<i>to our parade.</i>

01:21:14.570 --> 01:21:20.120
<i>Frankly, we were astonished</i>
<i>at the enthusiasm we encountered.</i>

01:21:20.290 --> 01:21:24.120
<i>If this humble servant of the theme park</i>
<i>going public has to go to jail,</i>

01:21:24.750 --> 01:21:30.050
<i>the positive reaction we received</i>
<i>will make it all worthwhile.</i>

01:21:31.720 --> 01:21:34.720
-What in the world?
-ls this for real?

01:21:34.890 --> 01:21:37.050
There's got to be some mistake here!

01:21:37.260 --> 01:21:41.220
<i>If this humble servant of the theme park</i>
<i>going public has to go to jail...</i>

01:21:41.390 --> 01:21:42.930
What an asshole!

01:21:45.520 --> 01:21:48.690
<i>This new development plunged</i>
<i>the raccoons into a state of panic.</i>

01:21:49.360 --> 01:21:52.150
<i>Meanwhile, Wonderland</i>
<i>was desperately searching for the people</i>

01:21:52.280 --> 01:21:54.450
<i>who staged the parade.</i>

01:21:54.570 --> 01:21:56.450
It's too late!

01:21:56.570 --> 01:21:59.490
Beat the bushes if you have to!

01:21:59.620 --> 01:22:02.160
Just find out who did it
and hire them all!

01:22:02.290 --> 01:22:06.080
Throw money at them!
I'll pay whatever they want!

01:22:06.210 --> 01:22:07.790
It was the work of raccoons.

01:22:07.960 --> 01:22:09.290
What's that? Raccoons?

01:22:09.420 --> 01:22:15.090
I don't care if it was penguins! I want
them all working exclusively for me!

01:22:16.760 --> 01:22:20.430
Raccoons? Wait a minute!
What's that supposed to mean?

01:22:20.560 --> 01:22:22.640
Oh, just a little joke.

01:22:23.060 --> 01:22:26.940
Who are you? How did you get in here?

01:22:27.020 --> 01:22:29.110
Your assistant let me in.

01:22:29.940 --> 01:22:32.610
I am Ryutaro.
We spoke on the phone earlier.

01:22:34.690 --> 01:22:36.610
This affair is a bit delicate.

01:22:36.700 --> 01:22:39.740
If you want to work
with the people who did this,

01:22:39.820 --> 01:22:43.080
I'm probably the only one
who can deliver them to you.

01:22:44.700 --> 01:22:46.830
Fine! I'll pay you 100 million yen.

01:22:50.540 --> 01:22:54.460
<i>The raccoons were dumbfounded.</i>

01:22:54.880 --> 01:22:57.680
<i>This bizarre human</i>
<i>had completely stolen their thunder.</i>

01:22:58.390 --> 01:23:00.680
<i>At first, they railed</i>
<i>against the unfairness of it all.</i>

01:23:00.760 --> 01:23:03.600
<i>But soon, the sheer hopelessness</i>
<i>of their situation</i>

01:23:03.680 --> 01:23:06.390
<i>began to sap their will to fight.</i>

01:23:08.020 --> 01:23:11.230
<i>Meanwhile,</i>
<i>with no footage of Operation Specter,</i>

01:23:11.310 --> 01:23:13.020
<i>media coverage petered out</i>

01:23:13.530 --> 01:23:16.990
<i>and the public</i>
<i>rapidly lost interest in the whole affair.</i>

01:23:31.540 --> 01:23:33.630
You're a fox!

01:23:36.260 --> 01:23:38.170
Truly, you have a discerning eye.

01:23:38.760 --> 01:23:43.010
I am Ryutaro, the shape-shifting fox,
at your service.

01:23:45.180 --> 01:23:50.190
I am honored to meet you, master Kincho.
I have heard much about you.

01:23:50.560 --> 01:23:53.480
I'm nothing more than the sixth
in a long line.

01:23:54.230 --> 01:23:57.030
And what business brings you here?

01:23:57.400 --> 01:24:00.280
I was amazed by your fabulous parade.

01:24:00.820 --> 01:24:02.910
At last, someone who understands!

01:24:03.320 --> 01:24:04.160
How could I not?

01:24:04.700 --> 01:24:08.290
And you have my deepest sympathies
for everything you've had to bear.

01:24:09.540 --> 01:24:15.670
I see... At least someone understands
what we're going through.

01:24:16.550 --> 01:24:19.920
And I was hardly surprised
by what happened after the parade.

01:24:21.220 --> 01:24:22.180
What's that you say?

01:24:22.760 --> 01:24:25.680
<i>Ryutaro the shape-shifting fox</i>
<i>could charm the birds from the trees.</i>

01:24:25.760 --> 01:24:28.220
<i>He convinced Kincho to come to Ginza.</i>

01:24:28.310 --> 01:24:31.350
<i>He showed the raccoon into a private room</i>
<i>in one of Tokyo's swankiest clubs.</i>

01:24:31.480 --> 01:24:32.730
Step right this way.

01:24:35.070 --> 01:24:38.150
Not to worry! All my girls are foxes.

01:24:42.240 --> 01:24:44.200
Do you like them this way?

01:24:44.280 --> 01:24:45.240
Would foxes suit you better?

01:24:45.660 --> 01:24:48.500
Or they can be raccoons, if you prefer.

01:24:51.000 --> 01:24:52.960
I'll get right to the point.

01:24:53.460 --> 01:24:55.590
There's no future
for the raccoons of Tama.

01:24:55.960 --> 01:24:58.210
They'll die out, just like the foxes.

01:24:59.380 --> 01:25:01.670
So that's what happened
to the foxes of Tama.

01:25:01.760 --> 01:25:03.470
Yes, I'm afraid so.

01:25:04.180 --> 01:25:10.140
The few of us who could shape-shift
have to live like this now.

01:25:10.560 --> 01:25:11.640
Among the humans?

01:25:12.060 --> 01:25:15.190
That's the only way to survive
in the big city.

01:25:15.560 --> 01:25:18.020
And that's why I invited you here,

01:25:18.110 --> 01:25:20.990
to recommend
that you raccoons do the same.

01:25:21.070 --> 01:25:22.950
Now hold on a minute!

01:25:23.030 --> 01:25:26.280
I know this must come as a shock,
but allow me to complete the picture.

01:25:27.370 --> 01:25:29.740
It's not enough
to start over in the human world.

01:25:29.830 --> 01:25:33.000
If you must swallow poison,
drink the whole cup.

01:25:33.080 --> 01:25:36.670
The best move would be for you all
to go to work for Wonderland,

01:25:36.750 --> 01:25:38.670
and solve your problem at once.

01:25:39.090 --> 01:25:43.680
You can't be serious! Work for the people
who made monkeys of us?

01:25:44.260 --> 01:25:46.010
Let's think about this calmly.

01:25:46.090 --> 01:25:48.850
It's time for you raccoons
to start living as humans.

01:25:49.100 --> 01:25:50.930
That's a foregone conclusion.

01:25:51.390 --> 01:25:53.940
<i>It takes big money to live like a human!</i>

01:25:54.020 --> 01:25:56.690
<i>And how do you make the money you need?</i>

01:25:56.770 --> 01:25:59.110
<i>You use the skills you have!</i>

01:26:00.440 --> 01:26:03.530
And who's going to pay the highest salary?

01:26:04.400 --> 01:26:07.530
I'm afraid that would be your enemy,
Wonderland.

01:26:08.030 --> 01:26:10.330
They tell me
they'll pay generous benefits too.

01:26:11.830 --> 01:26:15.920
Here's the salary,
and these are the benefits.

01:26:17.080 --> 01:26:20.960
Naturally, I'll be the only one
who knows you're raccoons.

01:26:25.550 --> 01:26:26.800
Please enjoy.

01:26:28.510 --> 01:26:31.350
Now then,
let's take our time and think this over.

01:26:31.430 --> 01:26:34.730
Master Kincho,
you must be used to eating better food

01:26:34.810 --> 01:26:36.480
than the scraps you get in Tama.

01:26:36.560 --> 01:26:38.770
I'm sure it's hard for you.

01:26:38.900 --> 01:26:40.060
That's not important.

01:26:41.360 --> 01:26:43.030
What I want to know is...

01:26:44.070 --> 01:26:47.110
The raccoons
who can shape-shift live as humans,

01:26:47.410 --> 01:26:50.070
but what about the ones who can't?

01:26:50.160 --> 01:26:51.990
They'll have to fend for themselves.

01:26:52.790 --> 01:26:57.210
The strongest genes must prevail
if the species is going to survive.

01:26:58.040 --> 01:27:01.750
We foxes had to abandon the others,
but we had no choice.

01:27:01.920 --> 01:27:04.460
And so... they died out.

01:27:04.840 --> 01:27:07.840
Yes, they did.
It was the choice we had to make.

01:27:11.930 --> 01:27:13.180
Ah, this is a tragedy!

01:27:14.680 --> 01:27:19.600
Well, you know, you raccoons
are omnivorous. Not like us foxes.

01:27:19.730 --> 01:27:23.190
Those who can't shape-shift
might not do so badly after all.

01:27:23.860 --> 01:27:25.990
<i>Meanwhile, the raccoons met once again,</i>

01:27:26.280 --> 01:27:31.450
<i>to consider what might be done</i>
<i>to improve their depressing situation.</i>

01:27:32.030 --> 01:27:34.290
<i>Only the core group came.</i>

01:27:35.620 --> 01:27:38.710
"We have a full array of potent tricks."
A load of hot air!

01:27:40.000 --> 01:27:43.210
We were idiots to think
those old dudes could help us.

01:27:44.500 --> 01:27:46.460
Reminds me of the saying,

01:27:46.590 --> 01:27:49.090
"Don't sell the pelt
till you catch the raccoon."

01:27:49.550 --> 01:27:54.560
No, I don't think even Buddha
could have seen how this would turn out.

01:27:54.640 --> 01:27:57.560
You shouldn't blame the masters.

01:27:57.640 --> 01:28:01.770
The humans say people like the president
of Wonderland are "sly as a raccoon."

01:28:01.940 --> 01:28:04.150
Humans are so weird.

01:28:04.480 --> 01:28:07.780
Speak for yourself, Shokichi.

01:28:08.240 --> 01:28:11.610
I just mean we need to do
a lot more research on the humans.

01:28:11.700 --> 01:28:15.740
Shut up! It's time to challenge them
to a fight to the death!

01:28:15.830 --> 01:28:17.830
Control yourself, Gonta.

01:28:18.080 --> 01:28:21.870
It seems to me
our only choice is to reveal

01:28:21.960 --> 01:28:28.340
that Operation Specter
was really staged by us raccoons.

01:28:28.760 --> 01:28:30.680
Have you lost your mind, Osho?

01:28:30.760 --> 01:28:34.220
We can't reveal ourselves to the humans.
It's an ironclad rule.

01:28:34.600 --> 01:28:40.350
She's right. If the humans knew
we did it, they'd hunt us all down.

01:28:40.890 --> 01:28:43.480
But it's so frustrating!

01:28:43.770 --> 01:28:47.860
Someone else
got the credit for all our work.

01:28:48.320 --> 01:28:51.860
I just can't accept it.
I want to tell the world!

01:28:52.030 --> 01:28:56.200
I want to shout it out! "We did that!"

01:28:58.080 --> 01:29:02.290
Master Osho, what could we do
to convince them it was us?

01:29:03.000 --> 01:29:06.130
All we have to do
is take public credit for it.

01:29:06.380 --> 01:29:09.630
Call the TV stations. Send out letters.

01:29:11.130 --> 01:29:14.640
They'd just think
it was somebody's idea of a joke.

01:29:15.140 --> 01:29:18.640
Then one of us should go on TV
and demonstrate for them.

01:29:18.770 --> 01:29:20.350
Nonsense.

01:29:20.680 --> 01:29:24.650
The humans would just think it was staged,
and we'd be humiliated again.

01:29:25.020 --> 01:29:27.020
You see? Talk is useless!

01:29:27.110 --> 01:29:32.900
<i>The debate dragged on through the night</i>
<i>and into the next morning.</i>

01:29:35.280 --> 01:29:38.080
You see? Talk is useless!

01:29:38.160 --> 01:29:42.120
But if we become terrorists,

01:29:42.460 --> 01:29:44.750
that will just incite
the humans to wipe us out!

01:29:44.830 --> 01:29:48.170
I keep telling you! We do it
without them knowing it was us!

01:29:48.250 --> 01:29:50.710
This means we can't do anything
that's really effective.

01:29:55.260 --> 01:29:59.350
Instead of going off half-cocked
in different directions,

01:29:59.560 --> 01:30:04.730
I think we should join forces for another,
even bigger Operation Specter.

01:30:06.350 --> 01:30:10.570
Where's the guarantee
we'll have a different outcome?

01:30:11.030 --> 01:30:14.820
All we have to do
is to get together like we did before.

01:30:15.240 --> 01:30:18.830
Ha! You're just playing around
in the sandbox.

01:30:19.200 --> 01:30:23.000
You're like a stinking girl!

01:30:23.200 --> 01:30:25.410
Watch your tongue, Gonta.

01:30:25.500 --> 01:30:27.040
That's no way to talk about women.

01:30:27.130 --> 01:30:31.130
Okay, but if he was a stinking girl,
that's what he'd be like!

01:30:31.210 --> 01:30:34.630
Anyway, I'm going to start getting ready
for Operation Specter part two.

01:30:35.170 --> 01:30:37.140
Yeah? You and who else?

01:30:38.180 --> 01:30:39.890
Do you think anyone'll follow you?

01:30:40.600 --> 01:30:41.600
What was that?!

01:30:41.850 --> 01:30:43.680
Moron!

01:30:44.600 --> 01:30:46.190
Knock it off!

01:30:48.900 --> 01:30:49.940
Listen everyone!

01:30:52.020 --> 01:30:53.440
There's only one way out of this.

01:30:53.570 --> 01:30:56.320
We have to use our shape-shifting skills

01:30:56.740 --> 01:31:00.830
like we did for Operation Specter!

01:31:02.330 --> 01:31:06.540
You know what kind of impact
Operation Specter had on the humans.

01:31:07.250 --> 01:31:12.800
But everyone thinks that idiot president
of Wonderland was responsible.

01:31:13.500 --> 01:31:15.840
So what can we do?

01:31:20.090 --> 01:31:21.850
How would you get
this egg to stand on end?

01:31:24.220 --> 01:31:27.440
This is how Columbus did it.

01:31:30.730 --> 01:31:32.360
Very impressive!

01:31:34.280 --> 01:31:35.860
You must have a really brilliant solution.

01:31:38.360 --> 01:31:43.200
It's time for us
to begin living as humans!

01:31:44.830 --> 01:31:46.450
No way!

01:31:47.080 --> 01:31:49.790
No, I'm absolutely serious.
This is not a joke.

01:31:49.920 --> 01:31:52.500
But what about the ones
who can't shape-shift?

01:31:53.670 --> 01:31:55.050
Where's Osho?

01:31:55.340 --> 01:31:58.220
APPEAL FROM 808 RACCOONS

01:32:01.050 --> 01:32:03.550
<i>With Osho gone,</i>

01:32:03.680 --> 01:32:07.680
<i>the raccoons could not agree</i>
<i>whether or not to follow Kinchi's plan.</i>

01:32:08.100 --> 01:32:10.390
<i>Their unity began to unravel.</i>

01:32:12.100 --> 01:32:16.780
<i>Operation Specter took precedence over</i>
<i>important matters like food gathering.</i>

01:32:16.860 --> 01:32:21.610
<i>Most of the raccoons turned to survival,</i>
<i>but Gonta began gathering followers.</i>

01:32:21.910 --> 01:32:25.080
<i>Meanwhile, age seemed to have addled</i>
<i>Master Hage's brain.</i>

01:32:25.160 --> 01:32:27.700
<i>He took in the raccoons</i>
<i>who could not shape-shift,</i>

01:32:27.790 --> 01:32:30.000
<i>and initiated them</i>
<i>into a Buddhist dancing cult.</i>

01:32:31.000 --> 01:32:34.040
<i>This world is an abyss, a mud boat</i>

01:32:34.130 --> 01:32:37.170
<i>Invoke the name of Amida and dance</i>

01:32:37.260 --> 01:32:40.260
<i>Namu Amida Butsu, this is the end for us</i>

01:32:40.420 --> 01:32:42.550
<i>Paradise will be our boat</i>

01:32:42.680 --> 01:32:46.260
Master Hage was always so hale and lucid.

01:32:46.810 --> 01:32:49.140
What an awful place Tokyo is!

01:32:49.640 --> 01:32:51.440
If Operation Specter
had taken place in Shikoku,

01:32:51.520 --> 01:32:54.610
the humans would have known
it was us raccoons.

01:32:54.770 --> 01:33:00.950
Offerings to us at shrines and temples
would have increased tenfold.

01:33:01.820 --> 01:33:02.820
Master Kincho!

01:33:03.990 --> 01:33:07.620
Master Kincho, my fervent desire
is to accompany you back to Matsushima

01:33:07.700 --> 01:33:09.830
and devote myself to training.

01:33:11.500 --> 01:33:13.830
Is that so, Tamasaburo?

01:33:13.920 --> 01:33:15.210
Yes.

01:33:15.750 --> 01:33:18.710
You're prepared to become my successor?

01:33:18.800 --> 01:33:20.510
Yes, Master Kincho.

01:33:20.920 --> 01:33:22.680
I've been waiting for those words!

01:33:23.260 --> 01:33:28.220
But you're not selfishly abandoning
your fellows

01:33:28.930 --> 01:33:33.850
to get back to Koharu, are you?

01:33:33.940 --> 01:33:36.730
Of course not, Master Kincho. Only...

01:33:37.060 --> 01:33:38.900
Only what?

01:33:40.480 --> 01:33:43.280
Even Master Kincho has lost the support
of the other raccoons.

01:33:43.900 --> 01:33:46.160
What purpose would it even serve
to stay here?

01:33:46.620 --> 01:33:49.160
I think there's something
we can do about that.

01:33:56.460 --> 01:33:59.380
Wow, this is quite an amazing restaurant!

01:33:59.800 --> 01:34:04.470
The owner has spared no expense
to make your visit a pleasant one.

01:34:09.970 --> 01:34:12.520
This place is really something!

01:34:12.600 --> 01:34:16.520
Good grief, it's better than Disneyland!

01:34:18.610 --> 01:34:21.070
A HUNDRED MILLION GOOD FORTUNES

01:34:37.750 --> 01:34:42.340
<i>And so Master Kincho</i>
<i>not only got his revenge on Wonderland,</i>

01:34:42.460 --> 01:34:46.550
<i>he obtained a massive war chest</i>
<i>for the raccoons.</i>

01:34:47.930 --> 01:34:51.260
<i>The president of Wonderland</i>
<i>rushed to the police</i>

01:34:51.350 --> 01:34:53.970
<i>to report the theft of 100 million yen</i>
<i>by a pack of raccoons.</i>

01:34:54.100 --> 01:34:55.680
<i>But no one would listen to him.</i>

01:34:58.690 --> 01:35:02.190
<i>Meanwhile, Gonta and his crew</i>
<i>of hardliners were taking steps</i>

01:35:02.270 --> 01:35:05.490
<i>to stop humans</i>
<i>from further clearing the forest.</i>

01:35:23.750 --> 01:35:25.710
<i>Attention, environmentalists!</i>

01:35:26.300 --> 01:35:31.220
<i>Stop interfering with our snake</i>
<i>extermination and leave immediately!</i>

01:35:32.180 --> 01:35:37.270
<i>You will be subject to prosecution!</i>

01:35:37.350 --> 01:35:39.770
<i>If you do not immediately</i>
<i>heed this warning and leave,</i>

01:35:41.270 --> 01:35:47.860
<i>we will use force to remove you!</i>

01:35:59.790 --> 01:36:04.000
<i>But Gonta and his army</i>
<i>ignored the warning.</i>

01:36:04.090 --> 01:36:06.630
<i>They pinned the police,</i>
<i>hunters and workers to the road</i>

01:36:06.710 --> 01:36:09.430
<i>and kept them from advancing an inch.</i>

01:36:09.510 --> 01:36:12.890
<i>And so both sides</i>
<i>continued the face-off as night fell.</i>

01:36:20.060 --> 01:36:25.360
What? If Gonta insists on doing this,
we ought to be standing with him!

01:36:28.360 --> 01:36:34.410
Can't you hear? The riot police
are already here. It's too late.

01:36:39.790 --> 01:36:41.670
I'm going to take a look!

01:36:41.750 --> 01:36:45.000
-Shokichi! They'll get you too!
-I'm going with him!

01:36:57.220 --> 01:36:59.560
-Ready, guys?
-Right!

01:36:59.640 --> 01:37:04.480
Even if we should fall
in the heat of battle,

01:37:04.980 --> 01:37:08.980
our deaths are certain to redouble
our brothers' resolve to carry on,

01:37:09.070 --> 01:37:15.120
till the day of victory dawns!

01:37:16.120 --> 01:37:21.040
<i>Our raccoon balls swing in the wind</i>

01:37:21.120 --> 01:37:25.790
<i>Back and forth, back and forth</i>

01:37:26.130 --> 01:37:30.090
<i>Amen</i>

01:37:30.170 --> 01:37:31.260
Special ops! Move aside!

01:37:31.340 --> 01:37:33.090
Gonta, wait!

01:37:33.590 --> 01:37:34.510
Move out!

01:37:51.940 --> 01:37:53.030
Gonta.

01:38:34.950 --> 01:38:38.820
<i>The raccoons used their family jewels</i>
<i>as weapons in a desperate kamikaze attack.</i>

01:38:39.830 --> 01:38:42.580
Mr. Raccoon, Mr. Raccoon.

01:38:44.580 --> 01:38:47.370
<i>Meanwhile,</i>
<i>in another part of Tama Hills,</i>

01:38:47.460 --> 01:38:50.040
<i>a reporter was trying</i>
<i>to interview the raccoons.</i>

01:38:50.130 --> 01:38:53.380
Mr. Raccoon, please come out.

01:38:53.460 --> 01:38:56.550
Any form you want to take is fine.

01:38:58.050 --> 01:39:02.970
The crew from <i>World TeleReporter</i>
is on your side!

01:39:07.100 --> 01:39:09.520
It looks like
they're not so eager to come out.

01:39:12.270 --> 01:39:17.070
<i>Mr. Raccoon, Mr. Raccoon</i>
<i>Why don't we talk?</i>

01:39:17.150 --> 01:39:20.780
<i>We've got nothing to eat</i>

01:39:20.870 --> 01:39:24.240
They answered! It's true after all!

01:39:26.040 --> 01:39:28.540
We'd like to hear
more about this from you.

01:39:28.620 --> 01:39:30.750
Won't you please come out?

01:39:30.830 --> 01:39:35.260
Oh! There they are!
It's the raccoons! It's them!

01:39:35.340 --> 01:39:38.630
Are you raccoons
really responsible for the specter parade?

01:39:38.720 --> 01:39:40.680
That's right!

01:39:42.300 --> 01:39:45.470
Please change into something
for our viewers.

01:39:45.560 --> 01:39:50.560
Otherwise no one will believe us.

01:39:51.150 --> 01:39:54.980
Some of us can't shape-shift.

01:39:55.150 --> 01:40:00.280
So if the woods are all gone,
we'll have nowhere to live!

01:40:07.410 --> 01:40:09.580
Raccoons, please listen!

01:40:10.370 --> 01:40:14.670
If you don't come out, this will make
our report look like fake news!

01:40:15.590 --> 01:40:18.880
If you want people to believe you,

01:40:19.170 --> 01:40:22.300
you'll have to show yourselves.

01:40:23.100 --> 01:40:24.100
Osho!

01:40:25.640 --> 01:40:29.520
Please go tell the humans everything!

01:40:37.360 --> 01:40:39.030
He came out! He came out!

01:40:39.110 --> 01:40:41.740
A ceramic raccoon is walking toward me!

01:40:48.830 --> 01:40:50.830
ACCOUNTING LEDGER

01:40:52.330 --> 01:40:54.960
Mr. Raccoon, a word for our viewers!

01:40:56.250 --> 01:41:00.470
We...we...

01:41:01.300 --> 01:41:02.340
Yes?

01:41:05.930 --> 01:41:06.930
Go ahead!

01:41:07.600 --> 01:41:08.810
Granny Oroku!

01:41:14.190 --> 01:41:16.570
It was us! We did that parade!

01:41:16.690 --> 01:41:18.900
These woods are our home!

01:41:19.360 --> 01:41:21.490
Please don't destroy them!

01:41:22.070 --> 01:41:24.740
We speak for every animal in the forest!

01:42:07.990 --> 01:42:12.000
<i>The person I saw yesterday is gone today</i>

01:42:12.080 --> 01:42:15.620
<i>The person I see today</i>
<i>Will be gone tomorrow</i>

01:42:16.380 --> 01:42:20.590
<i>Who knows what will happen to us tomorrow?</i>

01:42:20.670 --> 01:42:23.720
<i>Today everyone is sad</i>

01:42:23.800 --> 01:42:28.140
<i>Master Hage, last surviving witness</i>
<i>of the battle of Yashima,</i>

01:42:28.350 --> 01:42:33.810
<i>was 999 years old.</i>

01:42:34.180 --> 01:42:37.770
<i>But he had seen enough, and he</i>
<i>decided to bid the world farewell.</i>

01:42:38.650 --> 01:42:43.150
<i>With a song of triumph, the raccoons</i>
<i>stretched his vast testicles</i>

01:42:43.280 --> 01:42:46.530
<i>into a fabulous treasure ship,</i>
<i>with fittings of lacquer and gold.</i>

01:42:46.610 --> 01:42:47.870
TREASURE

01:42:50.160 --> 01:42:54.540
<i>Singing and dancing,</i>
<i>they boarded the ship,</i>

01:42:54.660 --> 01:42:59.080
<i>as they left behind a world</i>
<i>of suffering for the shores of bliss.</i>

01:43:00.090 --> 01:43:04.550
<i>The ordinary raccoons imagined paradise</i>

01:43:04.760 --> 01:43:09.430
<i>and boarded</i>
<i>as if they were going on an outing.</i>

01:43:12.430 --> 01:43:19.150
<i>The treasure ship set off down</i>
<i>the Tama River, swaying in the moonlight.</i>

01:43:19.230 --> 01:43:24.030
<i>The current bore the ship downstream,</i>
<i>the sail stood proudly in the breeze.</i>

01:43:24.320 --> 01:43:26.990
<i>The boat was full,</i>

01:43:27.530 --> 01:43:30.240
<i>the sail was flying high.</i>

01:43:30.320 --> 01:43:35.200
<i>Now the tide helped them forward</i>
<i>as the moon glinted off the water.</i>

01:43:38.540 --> 01:43:40.830
<i>The raccoons drummed on their bellies</i>
<i>as the ship sailed away,</i>

01:43:40.920 --> 01:43:43.590
<i>drumming and drumming</i>
<i>on this dreamy night.</i>

01:43:43.710 --> 01:43:46.970
<i>They celebrated with bells,</i>
<i>shamisen, flutes, and drums.</i>

01:43:47.050 --> 01:43:53.640
<i>The ship was laden with gold,</i>
<i>silver and precious coral.</i>

01:43:54.220 --> 01:43:55.850
<i>With tears in their eyes,</i>

01:43:55.930 --> 01:43:59.650
<i>the raccoons watching from the shore</i>
<i>prayed this would be no mud boat.</i>

01:44:01.520 --> 01:44:06.280
<i>As in a dream, the ship sailed on</i>
<i>past mist-shrouded woods and fields.</i>

01:44:06.360 --> 01:44:11.740
<i>The raccoons strained to catch a glimpse</i>
<i>of Amida beckoning from paradise.</i>

01:44:12.070 --> 01:44:15.240
<i>The treasure ship</i>
<i>crossed over to the next world.</i>

01:44:15.330 --> 01:44:18.370
<i>Singing and dancing, the raccoons</i>
<i>crossed over to the next world.</i>

01:44:18.460 --> 01:44:21.500
<i>With bells and flutes,</i>
<i>they crossed over to the next world.</i>

01:44:21.710 --> 01:44:25.500
<i>With samisen and drums,</i>
<i>they crossed over to the next world.</i>

01:44:25.590 --> 01:44:30.760
<i>They crossed over to the next world,</i>
<i>and they never returned.</i>

01:44:34.640 --> 01:44:38.730
You can't beat the humans after all

01:44:59.830 --> 01:45:02.420
Bunta, it's you!

01:45:03.580 --> 01:45:05.670
Bunta! Bunta!

01:45:06.170 --> 01:45:08.090
-Tamasaburo!
-Bunta!

01:45:11.220 --> 01:45:13.340
You've finally returned!

01:45:13.640 --> 01:45:14.970
Sasuke! Shokichi!

01:45:15.600 --> 01:45:20.600
Did you find Master Danzaburo?
Did you reach Sado and see the master?

01:45:21.560 --> 01:45:25.810
I learned at last
that he was shot by a hunter years ago,

01:45:26.440 --> 01:45:30.780
after the war, when food was scarce.

01:45:31.700 --> 01:45:35.410
How sad.
I was looking forward to meeting him.

01:45:35.990 --> 01:45:38.950
You did well, Bunta.

01:45:44.500 --> 01:45:49.590
What happened here in only three years?
I feel like Urashima Taro.

01:45:50.630 --> 01:45:52.920
We did everything we could to stop it.

01:45:53.010 --> 01:45:54.890
But everything has changed beyond belief!

01:45:55.180 --> 01:45:56.970
The land has shape-shifted,
not us raccoons.

01:45:57.050 --> 01:46:00.970
-We understand how you must feel.
-Did the humans really do all this?

01:46:01.560 --> 01:46:04.230
Yes, they did. They did it all.

01:46:04.600 --> 01:46:08.110
No, it can't be! Only raccoons
can change things like this.

01:46:08.520 --> 01:46:10.230
We're the only ones!

01:46:11.360 --> 01:46:13.780
The humans were really raccoons after all!

01:46:13.900 --> 01:46:17.820
Old, stinking raccoons!

01:46:19.660 --> 01:46:26.250
Give us back our woods! Give us back
our fields! Give us back our homes!

01:46:40.430 --> 01:46:42.020
Shall we give it one more try?

01:46:43.020 --> 01:46:47.190
Let's use the power we have left
to put everything back the way it was.

01:46:48.860 --> 01:46:52.230
We'll see who's better at shape-shifting.

01:46:52.360 --> 01:46:53.860
The raccoons or the humans.

01:46:55.240 --> 01:47:01.160
Sounds like fun! I can remember
every detail of the way things used to be.

01:47:01.280 --> 01:47:04.580
All right, then.
One last guerrilla attack!

01:47:05.040 --> 01:47:08.580
But what's the point?
It's already too late.

01:47:09.210 --> 01:47:12.050
Oh, it'll cheer us up.
That's all that matters.

01:47:13.300 --> 01:47:17.680
It's this playful spirit
that makes us raccoons, after all.

01:47:18.470 --> 01:47:20.970
Master Kincho, will you help us?

01:47:21.350 --> 01:47:25.480
Of course, though it may turn out
a bit like Shikoku.

01:47:26.390 --> 01:47:27.480
Ponkichi!

01:47:27.560 --> 01:47:30.560
Here I am! Shall I round up the others?

01:47:30.650 --> 01:47:32.520
Will you lend us your energy
one more time?

01:47:32.610 --> 01:47:33.980
You can rely on me!

01:49:29.180 --> 01:49:31.560
Wait up for me!

01:49:45.070 --> 01:49:47.620
Why, that's Mother!

01:49:50.250 --> 01:49:52.290
And Yotchan! It's Yotchan!

01:49:53.420 --> 01:49:55.500
Yotchan!

01:50:21.820 --> 01:50:24.740
That's us!
That's us when we were children!

01:50:32.450 --> 01:50:34.120
Look, raccoons!

01:50:34.330 --> 01:50:36.830
Wow! They're cute!

01:50:38.540 --> 01:50:40.210
Those are raccoons, right?

01:50:40.380 --> 01:50:44.800
I'm surprised to see them here,
so close to the city.

01:50:48.970 --> 01:50:51.310
Hey, raccoons! Don't go!

01:50:55.440 --> 01:50:57.310
Aw, they're gone.

01:50:58.310 --> 01:51:01.070
It would've been fun to feed them.

01:51:01.150 --> 01:51:04.320
I wonder if they can really shape-shift
like in the stories?

01:51:08.530 --> 01:51:10.780
<i>So in the end, we were defeated after all.</i>

01:51:11.410 --> 01:51:15.960
<i>Tama New Town kept growing</i>
<i>without the slightest hindrance from us.</i>

01:51:18.290 --> 01:51:21.540
<i>As the years passed, the city settled in</i>

01:51:21.800 --> 01:51:25.010
<i>and became a pretty nice place</i>
<i>for people to live.</i>

01:51:26.760 --> 01:51:31.760
<i>The hill where Manpuku Temple stood</i>
<i>is a trendy residential district.</i>

01:51:32.180 --> 01:51:36.020
<i>And I think our shape-shifting</i>

01:51:36.390 --> 01:51:40.230
<i>did have a good influence on the humans.</i>

01:51:41.060 --> 01:51:46.150
<i>As it said in the papers,</i>
<i>they're concerned about preserving nature,</i>

01:51:46.400 --> 01:51:49.280
<i>and they're setting aside</i>
<i>little bits of the woods for parks,</i>

01:51:49.360 --> 01:51:54.240
<i>"to live in harmony with the raccoons."</i>

01:51:55.450 --> 01:51:58.710
<i>But the parks were too late for us.</i>

01:51:59.000 --> 01:52:00.830
<i>They're too small for raccoons, anyway.</i>

01:52:01.580 --> 01:52:07.720
<i>Some of us moved further from the city,</i>
<i>where there were still woods and fields.</i>

01:52:08.340 --> 01:52:10.470
<i>But of course</i>
<i>there were raccoons there already,</i>

01:52:10.840 --> 01:52:14.220
<i>and with construction and the cars</i>
<i>that took one of us from time to time,</i>

01:52:14.350 --> 01:52:16.430
<i>life was hard.</i>

01:52:19.730 --> 01:52:23.980
<i>So we took the final step.</i>

01:52:37.660 --> 01:52:38.790
<i>That's right,</i>

01:52:39.250 --> 01:52:43.130
<i>those of us who could shape-shift</i>
<i>took a page from the foxes' book,</i>

01:52:43.210 --> 01:52:45.550
<i>and started living like humans.</i>

01:52:46.340 --> 01:52:49.800
<i>Nowadays I have a desk job</i>
<i>and my wife, Kiyo, works at a bar.</i>

01:52:50.760 --> 01:52:52.300
<i>A few raccoons got into real estate</i>
<i>and got rich</i>

01:52:52.680 --> 01:52:56.310
<i>selling forests to developers.</i>
<i>They're no different from the humans.</i>

01:52:56.680 --> 01:52:59.230
<i>Most of us are just worn out</i>
<i>from the stress of living in the city,</i>

01:52:59.310 --> 01:53:01.690
<i>and wish we could go back to the woods.</i>

01:53:03.440 --> 01:53:07.730
<i>I'm impressed by the humans.</i>
<i>It takes stamina to live the way they do.</i>

01:53:08.610 --> 01:53:10.780
<i>Some of us dropped out of the rat race</i>

01:53:10.860 --> 01:53:16.660
<i>and are scrounging out a living</i>
<i>on the streets.</i>

01:53:24.250 --> 01:53:27.460
<i>Oh, and what about Ponkichi</i>
<i>and the others who couldn't shape-shift?</i>

01:53:54.490 --> 01:53:58.330
<i>"Living for the moment"</i>
<i>is an expression made for raccoons.</i>

01:53:58.410 --> 01:54:01.910
<i>We never let property development</i>
<i>or accidents on the road get us down.</i>

01:54:02.160 --> 01:54:05.330
<i>We live as we please, relaxed</i>
<i>and joyous, in the present.</i>

01:54:05.420 --> 01:54:09.170
<i>We have children,</i>
<i>and we die, all too quickly.</i>

01:54:37.030 --> 01:54:38.740
Here I go!

01:54:42.370 --> 01:54:43.290
Woo-hoo!

01:54:58.850 --> 01:55:00.470
Ponkichi!

01:55:01.680 --> 01:55:03.060
Ponkichi!

01:55:03.140 --> 01:55:05.060
Shokichi!

01:55:08.230 --> 01:55:09.730
You came!

01:55:09.860 --> 01:55:10.900
How long has it been?

01:55:34.170 --> 01:55:36.050
You often hear on the news

01:55:36.130 --> 01:55:39.800
how foxes and raccoons are disappearing
because of urban development, right?

01:55:39.890 --> 01:55:41.890
I wish you humans would stop saying that.

01:55:42.430 --> 01:55:46.890
Sure, some foxes and raccoons
can shape-shift.

01:55:47.390 --> 01:55:50.770
But unfortunately,
most of us can't just disappear.

01:55:51.560 --> 01:55:53.610
What about the rest of the animals?
